{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_60", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -4 \"$TMPDIR/formal-fused-compact.log\"; git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "SBY  9:30:48 [reg_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY  9:30:48 [reg_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\n\nFormal: 53 passed, 0 failed\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/operand_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_operand_stage.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Exact MEM formatting fused into OC capture\n\nImplemented the requested local micro-optimization in `rtl/operand_stage.sv`\nand `rtl/core.sv`. OC receives the raw dmem word and the current EX/MEM\nregistered read/width/sign/lane metadata, plus the registered nonload ALU\nresult. MEM's existing post-trap/post-repair writer and readiness signals\nremain the authority for selecting a producer and qualifying capture.\n\nEach architectural source and each selected ALU operand has an independent\nfinal masked candidate reduction. The role's MEM enable is combined with\nword, byte, halfword, lane and sign controls before masking raw bits. Each\noutput bit includes at most seven distinct raw-bit candidates. Identical\nword/lane/sign contributions are folded into one scalar enable before the\nraw bit. No complete formatted MEM word or selected byte feeds a following\nOC role mux. Retained architectural sources use the same reductions. ALU\nroles read the saved, EX, MEM, WB, ID and PC/immediate candidates directly.\n\nPreserved all sequential OC capture, metadata, reset, hold, flush, advancement\nand saved-ready priorities. Producer priority and unavailable-producer\nblocking are unchanged. MEM formatting, its isolated bypass output,\nMEM/WB, bus effects, arithmetic, repair, divider, predictor, decoder, nret=1\nand top-level ports are unchanged. The original complete MEM bypass wire\nremains observable for verification but no longer feeds OC.\n\nExpanded the existing unit interface without removing its assertions.\nAdded exhaustive width/lane/sign and sign-boundary/one-hot raw-word checks\nfor all four roles, exact odd-lane/default-width behavior, accepted-load\nretention under changing raw words and metadata, and 6,000 randomized\ncomplete OC state-equivalence cycles. Pipe\n…[1263 of 4335 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1ef8c03e8c5fa754]…\n.934,\n  82.934 MHz; median 82.934 MHz. 4,119 logic cells, 1,329 registers,\n  8 LUT-RAM, 6 BSRAM, 6 DSP; reported worst paths now traverse EX\n  arithmetic/recovery into OC/frontend control.\n\nThe first implementation enumerated 32 sparse raw-bit terms per destination\nbit. It passed OC/pipeline and cosim but measured 81.529 MHz median and\n4,254 logic cells. Replaced that enumeration with at most seven relevant\nraw bits, preserving exact equations and folding duplicates. This is the\nonly implementation refinement; neither rejected MEM-only probe nor\npre-registered masks was used.\n\nThe measured result is a regression and does not meet the hypothesis's\nacceptance threshold (95.380556 MHz at unchanged bracketed cycles). The\nfitness is 197.62184 iterations/s and the acceptance ratio is 0.909504,\nbelow the required 1.046. The implementation is left for the orchestrator\nto evaluate; no performance\nwin is claimed. Additional candidate/control fanout and changed mapping\nof EX recovery paths remain the practical concern.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
