{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_92", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n# Shared, width-pruned combinational DIV/REM\n\nChanged only `rtl/alu.sv` and `test/test_alu.py`.\n\nThe four real division/remainder expressions now share one unsigned\nmagnitude divider. Its 32 generated restoring stages have a k-bit\ncandidate remainder and a k+1-bit subtraction. The subtraction's inverse\nborrow emits the quotient bit and selects the new remainder, with an explicit\nupper-divisor-bits-zero guard at every truncated stage. Signed DIV/REM\nnormalize operands, then correct quotient and remainder signs. Zero\ndivisors and INT_MIN/-1 retain the required RV32M results.\n\nTwo implementation refinements were needed beyond the initial plan:\n\n- The subtraction is biased by 2**k by setting its candidate's extra bit\n  to one. Its low k bits remain the exact difference, and its top bit is\n  one precisely when the k-bit subtraction has no borrow. This preserves\n  the fused subtract/select recurrence without a separate comparator.\n  The upper-divisor guard still examines every omitted magnitude bit.\n- Gowin `syn_keep` attributes preserve the normalized operands, each\n  difference, each partial remainder, and each subtract/select control.\n  The unannotated implementation reduced area but regressed Fmax to\n  3.615 MHz. Preserving these boundaries prevents costly factoring across\n  stages; the inverse-borrow encoding then improved the final median.\n\nAll multiplier expressions, base operations, ALU ports, pipeline logic,\nforwarding, stalls, retirement, and decoder legality checks are unchanged.\nThe complete RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch is byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\nThe ALU now conditionally includes the existing guarded core_pkg.sv when\nit has not already been compiled. This lets the requested alphabetical\nglob lint command work, while preserving existing package-first runners.\nExisting tests are retained; two new cocotb cases add 19,556 exact checks\nagainst an integer-only reference, covering all signed combinations,\nexceptions, large divisors, every power-of-two boun\n…[1127 of 4199 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6b7a6b1314384576]…\n | 5.442 | 5.888 |\n| Gowin placement option 2, MHz | 5.442 | 5.888 |\n| Median Fmax, MHz | 5.442 | 5.888 |\n| Fitness, CoreMark iterations/sec | 12.12 | 13.11 |\n| Bracketed cycles, 10 iterations | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\n| Logic cells | 12,312 | 3,667 |\n| Registers | 460 | 460 |\n| Option-0 worst arrival, ns | 199.837 | 177.159 |\n\nMedian Fmax improves 8.20%; reported fitness improves 8.17%, exceeding\nthe 4.6% threshold. Logic cells decrease 70.22%. LUT-RAM/BSRAM/DSP remain\n8/6/6. The final option-0 path has 499 cells and 189 reported logic levels,\nfrom cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0 to cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_26_s0, through\nforwarding and the execute ALU. Despite a higher raw cell count than the\nbaseline path, its measured delay is lower.\n\nConcerns: this remains a deep combinational divider; the measured benefit\ndepends on Gowin honoring the preservation attributes. Actual arithmetic\nis covered by exact tests and stalled cosim, not the ALTOPS formal gate.\nNo formal-deep arithmetic proof was run within this iteration.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
