{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git status --short; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_ex_divider.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_mem_repair.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Implementation notes\n\nImplemented the proposed address specialization exactly. `ex_mem_t` adds a\n32-bit `effective_addr` adjacent to `alu_result`. EX captures forwarded\narchitectural `rs1 + in.imm` directly into the existing instruction payload,\nwithout memory-op decode or general ALU/result selection. Existing whole-payload\nreset, hold, squash, divider snapshot and divider consume behavior includes it.\nMEM uses this registered field for bus addresses, byte masks, load extraction,\nalignment traps and aligned RVFI memory addresses. Ordinary result forwarding,\nmultiply validation and registered repair, store data, writeback, divider\ncancellation, branch behavior, nret=1 and ports retain their existing logic.\n\nUpdated packed EX/MEM layouts and standalone memory inputs. All prior assertions\nremain. Added checks for near/far address forwarding with negative immediates,\nevery load/store width and byte offset, misalignment suppression, eleven-cycle\nactive request holds, and address snapshot preservation through real/ALTOPS\ndivider completion and cancellation. Standalone MEM tests deliberately supply\ndifferent ALU results and effective addresses, including opposite alignment,\nand verify memory ports, RVFI masks/addresses, extension, ordinary writeback and\nheld WB payloads independently. Existing multiply repair/quarantine tests pass.\n\nNo RTL deviations or additional optimizations. The added address storage remains\nin both EX/MEM and the divider snapshot as requested. Inactive bus addresses may\nchange. Added storage and the exposed WB/branch recovery/training path remain\nthe main area/timing concerns.\n\nLocal validation:\n- Required Verilator lint: pass, no warnings.\n- All 15 pytest unit-test runners pass (four pipeline/MEM repair/real EX\n  divider/ALTOPS EX divider runners, plus eleven unchanged unit checks).\n  The cocotb result files contain 145 checks and zero failures.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: pass, both ELFs; selftest RVFI comparison\n  runs with and without stalls, and stalled CoreMark passes UART/CRC checks.\n- Unchanged `run_coremark_ipc`: completed ten iterations in exactly 4,201,709\n  bracketed cycles; canonical CRCs, validation literal, timing markers and\n  bounded accesses accepted by the validator.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`, placement option 0: 74.410 MHz; 3,910 logic cells,\n  1,067 registers, 40 LUT-RAM units, four BSRAMs, six DSPs. Worst path 18.733 ns\n  through WB, EX and conditional recovery/training, matching the measured probe.\n  Placement options 1 and 2 both measure 79.208 MHz. All placements pass;\n  median Fmax is 79.208 MHz. Combined with the unchanged bracketed cycle count,\n  fitness is 188.514 iterations/second; the required relative ratio is\n  `(79.208 / 75.013) * (4201709 / 4201709) = 1.055924 > 1.046`, and fitness\n  exceeds the 186.74238 floor.\n- Required `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`:\n  PASS on the first attempt, 53 passed and zero failed, with unchanged\n  single-channel ALTOPS gates. The final `reg_ch0` check passed after 492\n  seconds. No failure, counterexample or fix/retry attempt.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
