{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_63", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --untracked-files=all\nsed -n '1,200p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\nsed -n '30,96p' cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_fetch_predictor.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Predictor prediction/confidence planes\n\nThe final RTL replaces the 64 binary saturating counters in `rtl/if_stage.sv`\nwith packed 64-bit prediction and confidence planes. Each generated entry has\na constant six-bit training index and updates only on its local qualified EX\ntraining event. From the pre-edge state it computes `P_next = S ? P : T` and\n`S_next = !(P ^ T)`. Reset sets every entry to weakly taken (`P=1, S=0`).\nFetch dynamically indexes only the prediction plane. There is no dynamically\nindexed training read, increment/decrement, saturation comparison, shared\ncounter-result bus, additional stage, or delayed training.\n\nThe working tree initially contained this RTL and the requested transition\ntests. I reviewed them and strengthened the software-counter comparison to\ncheck both complete planes before and after training. These checks also\nverify confidence encoding, reset priority, disabled updates, and all\nunselected entries holding. The existing pipeline update assertion compares\nthe corresponding prediction/confidence bits with its original binary\ncounter model; all original predictor and pipeline assertions are retained.\n\nThe tests cover every entry, all four counter states, both outcomes, disabled\ntraining, saturation, alternating outcomes, deterministic interleaved indices,\nPC aliases, same-edge accepting reads/writes, and acceptance holds. No EX,\npipeline, arithmetic, memory, recovery, external port, or RVFI logic changes.\nThere are no architectural deviations from the hypothesis.\n\nValidation status:\n\n- Required Verilator lint: PASS, no warnings.\n- Predictor and pipeline tests: PASS (3 pytest checks).\n- Complete cocotb/pytest suite: PASS (17 pytest checks), including real\n  multiplier/divider arithmetic and decoder/trap checks.\n- Unchanged single-retirement ALTOPS formal gate: **53 passed, 0 failed** on first attempt;\n  no RTL fixes or retries. Command: `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=\n…[3902 of 6974 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4d37b25a1bdb3715]…\ns and training writes.\n  // Binary counter states 00, 01, 10, 11 map to (prediction, confidence)\n  // 01, 00, 10, 11. Confidence is local to each entry; only the packed\n  // prediction plane feeds the fetch lookup mux.\n  generate\n    for (genvar entry = 0; entry < 64; entry++) begin : g_direction\n      localparam logic [5:0] ENTRY_INDEX = 6'(entry);\n      always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n        if (reset) begin\n          prediction_q[entry] <= 1'b1;\n          confidence_q[entry] <= 1'b0;\n        end else if (branch_train_en && branch_train_index == ENTRY_INDEX) begin\n          prediction_q[entry] <= confidence_q[entry] ? prediction_q[entry]\n                                                    : branch_train_taken;\n          confidence_q[entry] <= !(prediction_q[entry] ^ branch_train_taken);\n        end\n      end\n    end\n  endgenerate\n\n  assign imem_addr = pc;\n\n  always_comb begin\n    out.pc    = pc;\n    out.instr = imem_data;\n    out.predicted_taken = predicted_taken;\n    out.valid = !flush;\n  end\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
