{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_87", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --short; python3 -c 'import subprocess; paths=[s[3:] for s in subprocess.check_output([\\\"git\\\", \\\"status\\\", \\\"--short\\\"], text=True).splitlines()]; assert all((p.startswith(\\\"cores/bench/rtl/\\\") and p.endswith(\\\".sv\\\")) or (p.startswith(\\\"cores/bench/test/test_\\\") and p.endswith(\\\".py\\\")) for p in paths), paths; print(\\\"All changed paths are allowed RTL or test files.\\\")'; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"", "aggregated_output": " M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n?? cores/bench/test/test_predictor.py\nAll changed paths are allowed RTL or test files.\n# Small tagged next-PC predictor\n\nImplemented the proposed 32-entry direct-mapped predictor, indexed by PC[6:2]\nwith complete PC[31:7] tags, valid bits, aligned targets and two-bit saturating\ncounters. Lookup uses only the fetch PC. Only valid bits reset; invalid entries\ncannot select uninitialized payloads. Conditional branches allocate at 2/1\nfor taken/not-taken, always storing the control target. Jumps allocate at 3\nand refresh their target. Conflicts replace tags and initialize a new counter.\n\nIF advances to the prediction only on accepted fetches. IF/ID and ID/EX carry\nthe exact selected successor. EX retains the existing forwarded comparisons,\ntargets, links and alignment traps, and compares the resolved architectural\nsuccessor against that metadata for every instruction. Repair and training\nrequire valid EX and no dmem hold. Repair wins over imem/load-use holds on\nrelease. Correctly predicted branches, calls and returns introduce no bubble.\nRVFI continues to report the actual successor and the original retirement\nboundary; nret=1 and all external ports are preserved. MEM/WB forwarding\nretention during dmem stalls and decoder legality are unchanged.\n\nMatching stale entries are invalidated for ordinary instructions and also\nfor illegal or unaligned controls. Allocation additionally checks source-PC\nalignment. Advancing FENCE.I clears all valid bits. These are conservative\nextensions of the proposed invalidation rules. Counter transitions use direct\nBoolean functions for the two bits; the CPU ALU and arithmetic are untouched.\nSeparate payload arrays with a common training enable gave better Gowin\nresults than a combined payload. A guarded core_pkg include also permits\nthe exact requested wildcard lint invocation.\n\nTests retain the original suite and add predictor reset/tag/counter/update\nchecks plus pipeline checks for warm loops/calls/returns, exits, JALR target\nchanges, aliases, stale instruction replacement, reserved control encodings,\nalignment traps, FENCE.I, imem and load-use recovery, dmem-held mispredictions,\none-time training, retained metadata and MEM/WB load forwarding. The local\nharness uses deterministic ready schedules and applies stores only on\naccepted handshakes. Every run checks RVFI order and architectural PC continuity.\n\nLocal verification: exact requested Verilator lint passes without warnings;\nall six pytest runners pass (91 cocotb cases). Unmodified `NRET=1 make cosim\nTARGET=bench` passes selftest under all bus-stall modes and canonical CoreMark\nCRC/validation checks. Final local formal status: PASS, 53 passed and 0 failed\nusing `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh`.\nEvery local formal run passed; no counterexamples or formal fix attempts\nwere needed. The unmodified full\n`NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` flow passes and reproduces the measurements\nbelow, including canonical CoreMark validation and all three placements.\n\nMeasured final-policy CoreMark count: 4,208,674 bracketed cycles for 10\niterations, versus the supplied baseline 4,491,485: 282,811 cycles saved\n(6.30%). Gowin placement options 0/1/2 report 5.303/5.568/5.568 MHz, median\n5.568 MHz. Area is 13,019 logic cells, 599 registers, 52 LUT-RAM, 6 BSRAM\nand 6 DSP. With the supplied baseline median 5.442 MHz, fitness is\n13.22982 versus 12.11626 iterations/s, a 9.19% improvement. This exceeds\nthe stated 4.6% threshold; acceptance remains the orchestrator's decision.\n\nRemaining concerns: direct-map conflicts and changing indirect targets still\ncause repairs. Gowin's worst path remains the forwarded combinational ALU,\nnot predictor lookup. The result applies to the unmodified measured CoreMark\nworkload; no return stack, history, cache or arithmetic changes were added.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
