{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261005-001-r9s0','hyp-20261005-002-r9s1']:\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(d['id'])\n  print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-001-r9s0\nReplace the serial OC source-forwarding, saved-source and ALU-operand\nmuxes with one mutually exclusive masked-OR candidate network per\ndestination. Keep the current ID/OC and OC/EX boundaries and every\ninstruction's advancement edge. Compute producer matches and readiness\nwith the current strict EX-over-MEM-over-WB-over-ID ordering. A matching\nunavailable nearest producer must block capture and must never select\nan older value. Readiness is control for capture, not another wide data\nmux. Preserve all valid, trap, x0 and recovery producer qualification.\n\nFor each architectural source, derive disjoint selects for the saved\noperand, current EX result, MEM bypass, WB result and ID snapshot. When\nits existing rsK_ready_q is set, select only rsK_value_q and disable all\nlive producer and ID candidates. Otherwise use the current forwarding\nwinner, with all candidates disabled for x0. Express rsK_value as one\nOR of the bitwise-masked candidates; remove the subsequent\nrsK_ready_q ? rsK_value_q : forwarded_value mux. Reuse this flattened\nresult for architectural source capture and one-time source retention.\n\nIndependently form each ALU operand directly from the same candidate\ndata, without passing through the architectural source-result mux.\nFor operand A, gate every register/saved-source candidate with\n!in.ctrl.is_auipc and add in.pc masked by in.ctrl.is_auipc. For operand\nB, gate every register/saved-source candidate with !in.ctrl.alu_src\nand add in.imm masked by in.ctrl.alu_src. Thus immediate and PC\nselection are absorbed into the one-hot enables ahead of the wide\nnetwork. Keep architectural rs1/rs2 independent of ALU operand\nselection, so stores, branches, JALR, multiplication and RVFI still\nreceive the exact resolved register values. Expose producer selects\nfrom forward_unit or extend its internal interface as appropriate;\navoid reconstructing another priority data mux in operand_stage.\n\nPreserve source retention while one operand is blocked or EX is held,\nclearing saved-ready flags on exactly t\n…[4138 of 7210 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:60698d3b848ae9d2]…\ne MEM/WB\nretirement, decoder/trap rules, memory alignment/side-effect checks,\nRVFI source values and strictly consecutive retirement order. No\nevaluation-contract path changes are proposed.\n\nValidate every source combination, saved-source priority, same-rd\nproducer shadowing, x0, architectural versus ALU roles, captured source\nretention and both recovery causes. Retain existing full-rate ALU and\nsingle-bubble load-use timing assertions. Run unchanged formal,\nready/stalled trace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/validation literal\nand MMIO brackets, and all three vendor Gowin placement options.\nAcceptance requires\n(Fmax_new / 85.344) * (4,196,601 / cycles_new) > 1.046;\nwith identical scheduling the median Fmax must exceed 89.270 MHz.\nThe expected gain is an estimate. Main risks are synthesis refactoring\nthe crossbar back into serial muxes, mask fanout, and another EX control\npath becoming dominant. Preliminary measurements will be recorded below;\nthey do not substitute for implementation-phase correctness gates.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
