{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r10s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r10s0',\n'title':'Use validity-only recovery for decode and operand payload registers',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion achieves 217.29 fitness at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its nine-cell data-RAM-to-OC path is now short enough that EX recovery and frontend register control are nearby limits. The full history was reviewed and LESSONS.md is absent. A local exact-load crossbar-fusion prototype kept the canonical CRCs and cycle count but regressed to 68.171 MHz; its worst path traversed EX recovery into ID across 37 cells. The r9s1 crossbar rewrite and r9s2 load predictor similarly exposed EX-to-ID/IF control paths. This proposal therefore targets the existing wide payload reset/enable muxes driven by late recovery, using the same invalid-bubble semantics already enforced by the pipeline's valid bits.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Separate decode and operand-stage payload updates from invalidation. Currently an EX redirect clears every bit of ID/OC and OC/EX and both retained source words, although only validity and saved-ready flags determine whether those words can be used. Remove flush from the wide data reset/select cones. Keep reset clearing, all capture boundaries, exact source routing and every instruction's issue/retirement edge. This is one micro_opt refactoring of pipeline register control, with no additional stage, prediction policy or arithmetic approximation.\n\nIn ID, generate the ordinary decode payload hold from id_ex.valid && (hold_oc_ex || \"'!operands_ready), independently of redirect. Wire that hold into ID for its payload update instead of the hazard output that is overridden on recovery. Reset still clears the complete bundle. Otherwise PC, instruction, raw sources, control, immediate, prediction and prepared operands update together only when this ordinary hold is false. The bundle'\"'s valid bit separately gives reset/flush highest priority, then accepts in.valid when the ordinary hold is false. Flush may leave arbitrary retained or newly captured metadata with valid=0; no late recovery signal may select zeros on these wide payload registers. Keep redirect-over-hold behavior for validity and fetch PC exactly as today.\n\nIn OC, keep current source matches, saved-source precedence, nearest unavailable-producer blocking and the flattened r9s0 candidate networks. When EX is not held, capture metadata and resolved architectural/ALU operands without first muxing an invalid, blocked or flushed payload to all zeros. Qualify only OC/EX valid with in.valid && operands_ready && \"'!flush. When EX is held, retain payload; flush must still clear valid immediately on the next edge. Invalid captured controls/data never authorize execution because all producer, divider, redirect, training, memory and retirement qualifications retain their current valid checks. Remove flush from the retained rs1_value_q/rs2_value_q word clears; keep saved-ready flags cleared on reset, flush and the existing advance edge. Saved data may capture or retain arbitrary unused values during a flush, but no stale word can be selected after its ready flag is cleared. Preserve one-time authoritative retention whenever a live blocked instruction has a resolved operand.\n\nAudit the existing consumers of invalid ID/OC and OC/EX bundles, including operand readiness, EX busy/result handshakes, target traps and source forwarding. Preserve or add scalar valid qualification where an invalid payload could otherwise cause a real effect; do not add a replacement wide output-zero mux. A bubble must produce no architectural write, divider launch, memory request, redirect, branch training or RVFI retirement. Older multiply repair still squashes younger work, beats irrelevant bus stalls and cancels any younger divider transaction. The original valid instruction payload and architectural operands must remain paired through every actual hold and both recovery causes.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and every external port, exact real/ALTOPS arithmetic, decoder default-illegal validation, branch prediction, memory alignment/side-effect checks, bus handshakes, full-rate dependent ALU forwarding, the accepted-load single bubble, sole MEM/WB retirement and consecutive RVFI order. No contract or benchmark changes are allowed.\n\nThe falsifiable prediction is identical bracketed CoreMark cycles and an eight-percent median Fmax/fitness gain. Acceptance at unchanged cycles requires median Fmax above 95.380556 MHz and fitness above 227.28534. This estimate needs vendor validation; nearby memory-return and EX arithmetic paths can cap the benefit. Test recovery simultaneous with ordinary holds, unavailable operands, imem/dmem stalls, saved-source retention and held divider completion. Update only incidental assertions that every bit of an invalid OC output is zero: require valid=0 plus disabled architectural effects instead, while retaining all assertions on valid payloads, real holds, reset clearing, exact forwarding, order and progress. Run unchanged formal, trace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/bracket gates and all three Gowin placement options.'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Separate valid reset/flush priority from wide payload updates. Keep reset clearing, use the ordinary redirect-independent stall for payload holds, and allow invalid payload bits to retain/capture without flush-controlled zero muxes.'},\n {'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'Remove flush and bubble-zero selection from OC/EX payload data and retained source words. Preserve scalar valid and saved-ready recovery priority, exact source retention, candidate routing and all real hold/capture edges; keep invalid payloads side-effect free.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire ID payload hold directly from the existing ordinary OC occupancy/operand-readiness condition, independent of the redirect override in hazard stall_id. Keep existing fetch acceptance, PC recovery, flush, producer eligibility, top-level ports and retirement wiring.'},\n {'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'Keep all valid-payload, saved-source, priority, readiness, reset and real-hold assertions. Replace only incidental invalid-bundle all-zero expectations with invalidity and side-effect checks. Exercise flush during holds and independently captured sources, then ensure fresh source selection after recovery despite stale retained words.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Check both recovery causes coincident with load/divider/dmem holds, invalid stale payloads encoding every effectful instruction class, exact surviving source fields and monotonic retirement. Retain full-rate ALU and one-bubble load-use timing checks, no wrong-path effects, decoder/trap checks and finite progress.'}\n]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
