{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m narrowing the final hypothesis to fusing MEM load formatting into OC’s existing candidate network. The MEM-only flattening probe still leaves a formatted return feeding another wide selector. This proposal removes that boundary while preserving the same acceptance edge and single load-use bubble. The expected gain remains unmeasured."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r11s0.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r11s0',\n'title':'Fuse exact MEM load formatting into OC operand capture masks',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 217.29 at median Gowin Fmax 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at data RAM and crosses MEM and OC into a multiplier operand register. OC already has a flattened forwarding/retention/ALU-role network, but an accepted load first traverses MEM lane extraction, sign/zero extension and load/nonload bypass selection before entering that network. LESSONS.md is absent; micro_opt history and recent outcomes were reviewed. The r9 OC flattening won, while r10 delayed load forwarding and validity-only recovery regressed. A fresh isolated MEM-only lane-mask rewrite passed 50,000 randomized complete MEM equivalence cycles but measured only 85.279 MHz median; pre-registering those masks measured 86.664 MHz. Those results reject those standalone changes and motivate removing the remaining MEM-to-OC selection boundary itself.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Make one local micro_opt change: fuse exact MEM load formatting and producer selection into OC's existing masked-OR operand capture networks. Retain the current pipeline boundaries, producer ages, bus acceptance and instruction advancement edges. Do not feed a complete formatted MEM load through another wide OC data-selection mux.\n\nSupply OC with the raw io_dmemRData word and the current EX/MEM registered load width, sign flag and effective-address lane, alongside the registered nonload in.alu_result. Keep MEM's original post-trap/post-repair bypass_writer and bypass_ready indications authoritative. These sidebands describe the same MEM instruction as those qualifications. The raw word is usable only on the existing accepted-load capture edge; it is never a predicted, cached, or separately accepted response.\n\nFor each OC destination role (architectural rs1, architectural rs2, selected ALU a and selected ALU b), combine that role's existing MEM select with mutually exclusive byte/halfword/word lane controls BEFORE the raw data masks. For ALU a/b, the MEM enable already includes \"'!is_auipc or !alu_src respectively. Form each destination'\"'s final balanced OR directly from its saved, EX, WB, ID and PC/immediate candidates, plus MEM raw-word/lane/sign candidates. Include sign extension within those candidates: upper bits select the original byte/halfword sign bit when mem_sext is set, otherwise zero. A word-load candidate uses raw word bits directly. A nonload MEM candidate uses the registered alu_result with the role's MEM select AND \"'!mem_read. Neither a selected byte nor a finished formatted MEM word may feed a following wide role mux. Shared scalar lane decodes are allowed; a shared complete 32-bit formatted result preceding the OC selectors defeats this hypothesis.\n\nUse explicit bit-slice equations, generated masked terms or equivalent balanced reductions so Gowin can map a raw bit or sign bit directly into the final candidate reduction. Fold identical raw-bit contributions together and avoid a serial procedural priority reduction or unnecessary duplicated 32-bit byte selectors. Use the same architectural source networks for one-time retained-source capture, so a load value saved while the other source waits survives changing bus data. The ALU-role networks must read candidate data directly, preserving r9'\"'s absence of architectural-value-to-ALU wide muxes.\n\nPreserve EX-over-MEM-over-WB-over-ID producer priority and saved-source precedence. A nearest unavailable producer still blocks capture; readiness qualifies the capture edge, never selects an older writer. Preserve x0, legal/trapping writer qualification, the current single load-use bubble and full-rate dependent ALU forwarding. Keep every OC metadata/control capture, reset, flush, saved-ready clear, hold and advance priority. Independent bus stalls, divider waits and older repair must never pair a raw word with another instruction's lane metadata.\n\nMEM retains its exact formatted read_data for MEM/WB architectural writeback and its existing isolated-module bypass_value behavior. Only the core's OC data wiring changes to bypass the complete MEM formatting result. Keep all memory-side address, replicated store data, byte masks, alignment traps, dmemReady qualification and registered multiply repair/quarantine unchanged. Older repair suppresses younger writers, captures and memory effects as today. Keep exact real/ALTOPS arithmetic, multiplication validation, divider start/hold/consume/cancel, branch prediction/recovery/training, decoder defaults and SYSTEM policy, nret=1 and every top-level port. Preserve original RVFI operands, exact load results/raw words/lane masks and strictly consecutive retirement order. No evaluator or other core changes are permitted.\n\nThe expected eight-percent gain has low confidence and is not a measured win. It targets a boundary that the measured MEM-only and predecoded-mask probes did not remove; neither failed probe should be implemented as the final proposal. More candidate terms and control fanout can negate the saved stages, and EX arithmetic/recovery can become the remaining limit. Scheduling should remain identical, but verify actual bracketed cycles rather than assuming them. Acceptance requires (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4,196,601/cycles_new)>1.046; at identical cycles this means median Fmax above 95.380556 MHz and fitness above 227.28534. Run unchanged formal, ready/stalled trace cosim, canonical 2K CoreMark CRC/UART/MMIO-bracket gates and all three Gowin placements. Retain every existing architectural, forwarding, hold, trap and advancement assertion.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'''Add internal raw MEM word and registered load-format sideband inputs. Replace each role's selected complete MEM value term with width/lane/sign/nonload terms whose scalar enables already include that role's existing MEM producer select. Fold these terms directly into the balanced final architectural/ALU candidate reductions. Preserve all other candidates, source retention, readiness, advancement, reset/hold/flush and metadata behavior. Do not build a shared formatted MEM word followed by the old role mux.'''\n},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire io_dmemRData and current ex_mem_w.ctrl.mem_read/mem_width/mem_sext/effective_addr[1:0] into OC, with ex_mem_w.alu_result as its nonload MEM candidate. Retain MEM's existing bypass_w_en/bypass_ready qualifications, EX/WB wiring and every top-level port. Leave mem_stage formatting and architectural MEM/WB behavior intact; its complete bypass_value no longer feeds OC.'''\n},\n{'file':'test/test_operand_stage.py','description':'''Adapt the internal unit interface while retaining all current forwarding, role, retention and recovery assertions. Compare fused capture against an independent exact load-format reference for every width/lane/sign and directed sign-boundary word, both sources and all ALU roles. Check changing raw words after a saved operand, unavailable nearest writers, x0, simultaneous holds/flushes, nonload results and instruction/metadata pairing.'''\n},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain full-rate ALU and single-bubble load-use timing assertions. Exercise signed/unsigned byte and halfword lanes and word loads feeding ALU, store, branch, JALR and MUL/DIV consumers with independent bus stalls, nearest same-rd shadowing, x0, saved-source retention and older multiply repair. Preserve all architectural, memory-side, trap, RVFI order and progress checks.'''\n}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final candidate written and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
