{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nids={'hyp-20261005-003-r4s2','hyp-20261005-001-r9s0','hyp-20261005-001-r10s0','hyp-20261005-003-r10s2','hyp-20261005-003-r11s2'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] not in ids: continue\n h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nids={'hyp-20261005-003-r4s2','hyp-20261005-001-r9s0','hyp-20261005-001-r10s0','hyp-20261005-003-r10s2','hyp-20261005-003-r11s2'}\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] not in ids: continue\n h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n print('\\\\n',d['id'],d['title'])\n print(h.get('hypothesis',h) if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n print('NOTES',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n hyp-20261005-003-r4s2 Predict the middle carry of EX arithmetic and validate full results in MEM\nAdd a stateless predictor for the carry or borrow entering bit 16 of\nEX ADD/SUB. Compute the low 16 bits exactly. Compute the upper 16 bits\nindependently using a predicted carry/borrow, instead of propagating a\ncarry across the full 32-bit forwarded-operand path. For ADD, use the\ncarry out of the four-bit window a[15:12]+b[15:12]+seed. The seed is one\nwhen either operand's low 12 bits are all ones and the other operand's\nlow 12 bits are nonzero, otherwise zero. This inexpensive special case\nhandles common decrement-by-one arithmetic without a full lower-half\ncarry chain. For SUB, predict a borrow when a[15:12] < b[15:12], assuming\nno borrow into the window. Compute upper ADD as a[31:16]+b[31:16]+carry\nand upper SUB as a[31:16]-b[31:16]-borrow, modulo 16 bits. Implement\neach upper operation as one 17-bit two-operand chain: upper ADD is\nbits [16:1] of {a[31:16],1'b1}+{b[31:16],carry}, and upper SUB is\nbits [16:1] of {a[31:16],1'b0}-{b[31:16],borrow}. Avoid a three-operand\nexpression that can infer two serial 16-bit adders. These are fallible\npredictions, not replacements for architectural arithmetic.\n\nPut the predicted 32-bit result in EX/MEM so the ordinary forwarding\npath can supply it to the immediately following instruction. Preserve\nthe original full-width forwarded rs1/rs2, PC, instruction and controls.\nAlso capture the already-selected full-width alu_a and alu_b and the\nsingle predicted carry/borrow bit into EX/MEM. AUIPC's base is PC;\nADDI/load/store use their correctly sign-extended I/S immediate;\nregister ADD/SUB use rs2. Exact MEM arithmetic consumes those registered\noperands directly; do not recreate immediate decode or operand muxes\nahead of MEM validation. A shared exact 32-bit add/sub datapath supplies\nthe architectural result. Correct only\nADD, ADDI, AUIPC, SUB and load/store address computations. JAL/JALR\nretain their PC+4 link values even though their decoder's default ALU\noperation is ADD. Branches,\n…[21360 of 24432 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d36ca18180476bb3]…\nted by the existing MEM-to-OC or EX recovery path,\nand physical placement can outweigh the small predictor area reduction;\nno win is claimed before implementation-phase evaluation.\n\nPreserve nret=1, all external ports, exact RVFI operands/results/order,\ndecoder defaults and trap discipline, memory side effects, divider\ntransaction/cancellation and real/ALTOPS arithmetic, and every hard\ninvariant. Exhaustively compare all four states and both outcomes with\nthe original saturating-counter transition model, then test disabled\ntraining, reset, saturation, alternating outcomes, aliases, same-edge\nlookup/update and acceptance holds. Retain every existing predictor and\npipeline assertion. Run unchanged formal, ready/stalled trace cosim,\ncanonical 2K CoreMark CRC/bracket/completion validation and all three\nGowin placements. Expected bracketed cycles are exactly 4196601.\nAt unchanged cycles, acceptance requires median Fmax above 95.380556 MHz;\nin general require (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046.\n\nNOTES \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
