The raw word is usable only on the existing accepted-load capture edge; it is never a predicted, cached, or separately accepted response.\n\nFor each OC destination role (architectural rs1, architectural rs2, selected ALU a and selected ALU b), combine that role's existing MEM select with mutually exclusive byte/halfword/word lane controls BEFORE the raw data masks. For ALU a/b, the MEM enable already includes !is_auipc or !alu_src respectively. Form each destination's fina\n…[1319 of 4391 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7f9c0c02092ef660]…\nce. A nearest unavailable producer still blocks capture; readiness qualifies the capture edge, never selects an older writer. Preserve x0, legal/trapping writer qualification, the current single load-use bubble and full-rate dependent ALU forwarding. Keep every OC metadata/control capture, reset, flush, saved-ready clear, hold and advance priority. Independent bus stalls, divider waits and older repair must never pair a raw word with another instruction's lane metadata.\n\nMEM retains its exact formatted read_data for MEM/WB architectural writeback and its existing isolated-module bypass_value behavior. Only the core's OC data wiring changes to bypass the complete MEM formatting result. Keep all memory-side address, replicated store data, byte masks, alignment traps, dmemReady qualification and registered multiply repair/quarantine unchanged. Older repair suppresses younger writers, captures and memory effects as today. Keep exact real/ALTOPS arithmetic, multiplication validation, divider start/hold/consume/ca\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
