{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'source|unused|false|rs2|operand.*use' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl --only-matching | sort -u | head -80; ls -la cores/bench/experiments\"", "aggregated_output": "10:operand\\nselection, EX forwarding, a full-width DSP multiplier and ALU selection,\\nthen the data-memory address port. This is a physical timed path even\\nthough multiplication instructions do not perform data-memory accesses.\\nThe canonical CoreMark ELF executes 93,960 MULs between the MMIO markers;\\nevery one has the same low-32-bit result as a signed 16-by-16 product.\\nThere are 35,640 immediate raw source dependencies after these MULs.\\nThese observations favor computational value prediction over a larger\\nbranch predictor: shorten the timed EX product path while preserving\\nsingle-cycle predicted-result forwarding for the common operand range.\\nA temporary prototype outside the core source tree was evaluated with the\\nunchanged harness. Gowin placement options 0/1/2 reached 52.548/54.014/\\n54.014 MHz, median 54.014 MHz. Stalled CoreMark retained exactly 4,201,709\\ncounted cycles, all five canonical CRCs, the required validation literal,\\nand oob=false. The resulting projected fitness is 128.55, about 9.2 percent\\nabove 117.75. Existing selftest and all three random-program cosim checks\\npassed both zero-wait and imem/dmem-stalled runs, with field-by-field ISS\\ncomparison. This evidence is for a temporary prototype; the hypothesis\\nimplementation must still pass unchanged formal and unit-test gates.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The champion scores 117.75 at median Fmax 49.474 MHz and 4,201,709\\ncounted CoreMark cycles. Both prior predictor attempts were reviewed in\\nlog.jsonl; LESSONS.md is absent. The current 64-entry bimodal predictor\\nalready removes most taken-control bubbles. A new read-only architectural\\nprofile found 135,320 immediate load-to-branch dependencies, too few for\\ntheir removal alone to exceed the 184,779-cycle acceptance requirement at\\nunchanged Fmax. Improving branch direction alone has still less headroom.\\nA fresh unchanged-core Gowin option-0 run reproduces 50.610 MHz and the\\n25.054 ns worst arrival path: register-file BRAM output through ID operand\\nselection, EX forwarding,\n…[244772 of 247844 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f2271f1f13ff53da]…\nce. Actual dmem stalls still hold EX/MEM and preserve\\nWB forwarding data. Arithmetic continues independently after launch;\\na completed result and its original forwarded operand snapshots remain\\nstable until downstream acceptance. Transfer the completed payload into\\nEX/MEM exactly once and release ID/EX on that same edge. Keep busy set\\nthrough consumption so the held instruction cannot restart. A following\\ndependent instruction receives the result through normal forwarding.\\nDo not launch twice, replay an older memory request, train a held branch,\\nor allow a waiting instruction's changing forwarding muxes to alter an\\noutstanding transaction. Reuse\n9:source\ntotal 516\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup   4096 Oct  5 10:21 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup   4096 Oct  5 10:21 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup      0 Oct  5 10:21 .gitkeep\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup   4096 Oct  5 10:21 hypotheses\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 419164 Oct  5 10:21 log.jsonl\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  80028 Oct  5 10:21 progress.png\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
