{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] in ['hyp-20261005-002-r9s1','hyp-20261005-001-r11s0','hyp-20261005-002-r8s1']:\n  print(d['id'],d['title']);print(d['hypothesis']['motivation']);\n  if 'r9s1' in d['id']:print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\nsed -n '1,260p' tools/eval/gowin.py; sed -n '1,150p' cores/bench/test/conftest.py; sed -n '1,170p' cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-002-r8s1 Split operand collection from execution with an EX-result return bypass\nThe champion scores 188.51 at median 79.208 MHz and 4,201,709 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Structural history favors register\nboundaries: ID operand/bypass retiming and registered multiply recovery\nwon, while the eight-entry fetch queue and the early registered-redirect\nexperiment lost fitness. A fresh vendor placement-option-1 build\nreproduces 79.208 MHz. Its worst paths include registered forwarding\nselectors through branch resolution into predictor counters, and the\nWB result mux through EX forwarding and the narrow multiplier into\nEX/MEM. Moving only predictor training, flattening the WB bypass into\ntyped lanes, and replicating branch comparators did not improve vendor\ntiming in isolated probes. A registered control-flow probe passed all\neight ready/stalled trace comparisons and canonical CoreMark validation,\nbut cost only 1.52 percent more bracketed cycles with today's predictor.\nThe most promising remaining structural angle is a real operand/\nexecution pipeline boundary, which cuts forwarding off both arithmetic\nand branch-resolution inputs while preserving dependent ALU throughput.\n\nhyp-20261005-002-r9s1 Unify retained sources and bypass routing in the OC capture crossbar\nThe champion scores 203.3