{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(s)\n if d['id']=='hyp-20261005-001-r11s0':\n  h=d['hypothesis']\n  print(h['motivation'])\n  print(json.dumps(h['changes'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"The champion scores 217.29 at median Gowin Fmax 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its reported worst path starts at data RAM and crosses MEM and OC into a multiplier operand register. OC already has a flattened forwarding/retention/ALU-role network, but an accepted load first traverses MEM lane extraction, sign/zero extension and load/nonload bypass selection before entering that network. LESSONS.md is absent; micro_opt history and recent outcomes were reviewed. The r9 OC flattening won, while r10 delayed load forwarding and validity-only recovery regressed. A fresh isolated MEM-only lane-mask rewrite passed 50,000 randomized complete MEM equivalence cycles but measured only 85.279 MHz median; pre-registering those masks measured 86.664 MHz. Those results reject those standalone changes and motivate removing the remaining MEM-to-OC selection boundary itself.\n[\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/operand_stage.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Add internal raw MEM word and registered load-format sideband inputs. Replace each role's selected complete MEM value term with width/lane/sign/nonload terms whose scalar enables already include that role's existing MEM producer select. Fold these terms directly into the balanced final architectural/ALU candidate reductions. Preserve all other candidates, source retention, readiness, advancement, reset/hold/flush and metadata behavior. Do not build a shared formatted MEM word followed by the old role mux.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Wire io_dmemRData and current ex_mem_w.ctrl.mem_read/mem_width/mem_sext/effective_addr[1:0] into OC, with ex_mem_w.alu_result as its nonload MEM candidate. Retain MEM's existing bypass_w_en/bypass_ready qualifications, EX/WB wiring and every top-level port. Leave mem_stage formatting and architectural MEM/WB behavior intact; its complete bypass_value no longer feeds OC.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_operand_stage.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Adapt the internal unit interface while retaining all current forwarding, role, retention and recovery assertions. Compare fused capture against an independent exact load-format reference for every width/lane/sign and directed sign-boundary word, both sources and all ALU roles. Check changing raw words after a saved operand, unavailable nearest writers, x0, simultaneous holds/flushes, nonload results and instruction/metadata pairing.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Retain full-rate ALU and single-bubble load-use timing assertions. Exercise signed/unsigned byte and halfword lanes and word loads feeding ALU, store, branch, JALR and MUL/DIV consumers with independent bus stalls, nearest same-rd shadowing, x0, saved-source retention and older multiply repair. Preserve all architectural, memory-side, trap, RVFI order and progress checks.\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
