{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"agent_message","text":"The remaining probes also lowered Fmax. I’m finalizing a different, unmeasured hypothesis: fold EX’s jump-link, multiply and ordinary-result selection into OC’s existing forwarding masks. This targets two serial result muxes on the champion’s EX return path. The expected gain will remain explicitly low-confidence."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_62", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport yaml\nimport jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r15s0.yaml')\ncontent='''id: hyp-20261005-001-r15s0\ntitle: \\\"Fold EX result classes directly into OC forwarding masks\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion achieves 217.29 fitness at median Gowin Fmax 91.186 MHz\n  with 4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent; the\n  micro_opt history and recent outcomes were reviewed. A fresh baseline\n  timing run reproduced 87.616/91.186/91.186 MHz. In placement options\n  1 and 2 the worst path starts at an EX ALU operation register, crosses\n  the inferred arithmetic and OC data selection, and ends at the narrow\n  multiplier's absorbed operand register. EX currently selects jump link,\n  predicted product or ordinary ALU result before OC selects that producer.\n  The r9 improvement removed serial saved-source and ALU-role muxes in OC,\n  but left this upstream EX result-selection boundary intact.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make one local exact micro-optimization: absorb EX's outer result-class\n  selection into OC's existing mutually exclusive forwarding masks.\n  Preserve every pipeline stage, advancement edge, bus handshake and\n  prediction policy. Do not register a new result or add a dependency\n  bubble. The intended physical change is removal of the serial wide\n  jump/multiply selections between EX arithmetic and OC capture.\n\n  Export three unselected EX candidates: the existing ordinary ALU\n  result, the existing predicted multiplication result, and PC+4 link.\n  Also export the current registered instruction's is_jump and is_mul\n  classifications. Keep the existing final, post-trap bypass_w_en and\n  bypass_ready authoritative. The ordinary candidate includes the held\n  divider result exactly as today; it must not become usable before the\n  existing divider completion. No new arithmetic or prediction is added.\n\n  For each OC destination role, replace its single masked ex_value term\n  with three disjoint terms. If E is that role's existing EX select, use\n  E && is_jump for the link, E && \"'!is_jump && is_mul for the product, and\n  E && !is_jump && !is_mul for the ordinary ALU result. Form these scalar\n  enables before the wide data masks, then combine the three candidates\n  directly with that role'\"'s saved, MEM, WB, ID and PC/immediate candidates\n  in its final OR reduction. For ALU A/B, E already incorporates the\n  existing AUIPC/immediate restrictions. Jump selection must retain its\n  current precedence. Use balanced reductions; do not reconstruct a\n  shared selected EX word followed by another role mux, or an EX-only\n  wide reduction followed by the original producer-selection mux.\n\n  Apply the same expanded architectural-source networks to one-time\n  saved-source capture. Preserve saved-source precedence, strict nearest\n  EX-over-MEM-over-WB-over-ID priority, unavailable-producer blocking,\n  x0, independently retained operands and all capture/hold/reset/flush\n  rules. The scalar producer and result-class selects must describe the\n  same current EX instruction as the candidate data. Preserve full-rate\n  dependent ALU issue and the accepted-load single dependency bubble.\n  Keep MEM load formatting and its complete bypass interface unchanged.\n\n  EX/MEM still captures the original selected result on its existing\n  edge; its payload, divider transactions and cancellation, exact MEM\n  multiplication validation, registered repair and younger-memory\n  quarantine remain intact. Keep all target/address arithmetic, branch\n  comparison, prediction, redirects, training, alignment traps, decoder\n  default-illegal validation and SYSTEM policy. Preserve real/ALTOPS\n  arithmetic, nret=1, every external port, exact RVFI source snapshots,\n  results, successors, memory records and consecutive retirement order.\n  Change only the listed allowed RTL and cocotb files.\n\n  Expect an eight-percent fitness gain with low confidence and unchanged\n  counted cycles. This final EX-to-OC fusion has not been implemented or\n  measured. Do not substitute the measured rejected probes: balanced\n  byte comparisons reached 77.661 MHz median, a shared signed multiplier\n  81.350 MHz, registered multiplier sign bits 81.642 MHz, a dedicated\n  ADD/SUB control 79.475 MHz, branch predicate factoring 82.037 MHz and\n  a shared barrel shifter 77.306 MHz. The prior r14 registered one-hot\n  selector also regressed; this proposal instead removes the EX/OC\n  selection boundary while retaining binary ALU decoding and arithmetic.\n  The r11 MEM-load fusion is also excluded: it expanded raw byte/lane\n  formatting into OC, whereas this change adds only two EX result terms.\n\n  More mask terms, synthesis refactoring, branch recovery and the remaining\n  MEM-return path can outweigh the removed muxes. Inspect the Gowin mapped\n  paths to verify the three raw EX candidates reach the final role masks\n  without an intermediate class-selected data word. Require\n  (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046. At unchanged cycles,\n  acceptance requires median Fmax above 95.380556 MHz and fitness above\n  227.28534. Run unchanged formal, unit, ready/stalled field-by-field\n  cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/UART/MMIO-bracket checks and all three\n  vendor Gowin placements. Preserve every architectural and advancement\n  assertion; report actual cycles and median fitness before claiming a win.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Export ordinary ALU/divider, predicted multiplication and PC+4 link\n      candidates with current EX jump/multiply classifications for OC.\n      Retain existing bypass eligibility/readiness, selected EX/MEM\n      result capture and all arithmetic, recovery and training behavior.\n  - file: rtl/operand_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Replace the single selected EX data input in each architectural\n      and ALU-role crossbar with three raw candidates whose scalar masks\n      incorporate its existing EX select and jump/multiply precedence.\n      Fold them directly into balanced final role reductions, including\n      one-time source retention. Preserve all other candidates, producer\n      priority, readiness, saved values, metadata and register controls.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the three raw EX candidates and result-class sidebands to OC\n      in place of its selected EX value input. Preserve all existing\n      qualification, hazard, memory, divider, repair and RVFI wiring,\n      pipeline boundaries and the complete nret=1 external interface.\n  - file: test/test_operand_stage.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt the internal EX candidate interface while retaining all\n      current assertions. Check each class against independently\n      selected expected values for both sources and all ALU roles,\n      including jump precedence, x0, unavailable nearest writers,\n      saved-source overrides, changing candidates and holds/flushes.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every architectural, full-rate ALU and single-bubble\n      load-use assertion. Exercise EX arithmetic, all multiplication\n      variants, jump links and held divider completion feeding ALU,\n      store, branch, JALR and arithmetic consumers. Cover bus stalls,\n      nearest same-rd shadowing, source retention and multiply repair\n      with exact RVFI operands/results/successors and consecutive order.\n'''\nd=yaml.safe_load(content)\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261005-001-r15s0'\nassert d['category']=='micro_opt'\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert -50 <= d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct'] <= 50\nstaging=p.with_suffix('.yaml.next')\nstaging.write_text(content)\nstaging.replace(p)\nprint(f'Written and schema-validated: {p}')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
