{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r3s0.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-001-r3s0\ntitle: \"Collapse cascaded execute operand muxes into parallel one-hot selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion scores 117.75 at 49.474 MHz and 4,201,709 measured\n  CoreMark cycles. Its worst reported path is 25.054 ns with 14 cells,\n  from the register file through decode, execute and the ALU to memory.\n  The previous micro_opt attempts targeted the combinational divider and\n  redirect control; the divider is now iterative and redirect cleanup\n  alone did not deliver a competitive improvement. No LESSONS.md exists.\n  EX currently selects a forwarded source and then selects PC/immediate\n  operands, adding serial muxes before every arithmetic operation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the cascaded EX forwarding and ALU-source muxes with a single\n  parallel one-hot operand-selection network per ALU input. For operand\n  A, derive mutually exclusive selections for PC on AUIPC, the EX/MEM\n  forwarded value, the MEM/WB forwarded value, and the captured rs1 value.\n  For operand B, select immediate when alu_src is set; otherwise select\n  the freshest rs2 value from EX/MEM, MEM/WB, or ID/EX. Express each operand\n  as an OR of bitwise-masked candidates so FPGA LUTs can combine source\n  qualification and data selection, rather than placing a forwarding\n  mux followed by a PC/immediate mux on the arithmetic input path.\n\n  Make forwarding produce independent one-hot enables with explicit\n  EX/MEM-over-MEM/WB priority and x0 exclusion. Retain separately selected\n  architectural rs1 and rs2 values for branch comparison, JALR, stores,\n  division operand capture and RVFI; PC/immediate selection must never\n  substitute for these architectural source values. Keep retained WB\n  forwarding available during dmem holds even when WB valid has cleared,\n  as required by the existing stall protocol. Preserve bubble producer\n  controls and the current treatment of all valid and illegal encodings.\n\n  This changes combinational selection only: retain the current pipeline\n  registers, single-cycle mu\n…[1261 of 4333 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3ed547345095c76a]…\ng exclusive enables. Keep independent\n      architectural-source selections for branch/JALR/store/RVFI and\n      capture the same forwarded operands for the existing divider.\n      Preserve EX/MEM holds, divider bubbles, completion, redirects,\n      prediction training, link writes and all alignment traps.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Wire the internal forwarding enables to EX while retaining every\n      external port, stage boundary, hazard action and RVFI field.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Retain existing tests and add directed simultaneous EX/MEM and\n      MEM/WB matches to the same source, independent matches on rs1/rs2,\n      x0 writes, AUIPC and immediate instructions with aliased raw source\n      fields, and load-to-dependent operations held by dmem stalls.\n      Verify arithmetic results, architectural RVFI source values,\n      store data, branch/JALR targets, divider operand capture and unique\n      retirement order under always-ready and stalled buses.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
