Hz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA comb\n…[173252 of 176324 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:50822a3de9b85bbf]…\nration\\n  validated.\\\", and no out-of-bounds access occurred.\\n\\n## Final vendor timing and acceptance\\n\\nGowin placement options 0/1/2 measured 59.447/59.885/59.885 MHz; median Fmax\\nis 59.885 MHz. Area is 3,629 logic cells, 1,023 registers, eight LUT-RAMs,\\nsix BSRAMs and six DSPs. The worst median-placement path now passes through\\nthe existing narrow multiplication predictor rather than a full-width EX\\nright shifter; the worst reported arrival is 21.993 ns.\\n\\nStalled CoreMark start/stop cycles are 15,885 and 4,291,364. Only their\\ndifference, 4,275,479 cycles, counts. This is 73,770 cycles above the champion.\\n\\nAcceptance ratio = (59.885 / 58.252) * (4,201,709 / 4,275,479)\\n                 = 1.01029547.\\n\\nThis implementation is correct under the completed local checks but DOES NOT\\nmeet the required ratio greater than 1.046. The approximately 1.03% fitness\\nincrease is insufficient; do not classify this hypothesis as accepted.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T03:18:22.007060Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 5}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
