fore the subtraction.\n\nNormalize operands to unsigned magnitudes only for signed DIV/REM, then\nrestore the quotient sign from the operand-sign XOR and the remainder\nsign from the dividend. Select the signed or unsigned quotient/remainder\nat the existing ALU output. Preserve divide-by-zero results, INT_MIN/-1,\ntruncation toward zero, and dividend-signed remainders exactly. Keep all\nRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS formulas byte-for-byte equivalent to the baseline.\nThis is solely a combinational arithmetic refactoring: retain the ALU\ninterface, execution latency, forwarding, bus handshakes, retirement\nwidth, decoder legality checks, and all other operations. The prediction\nis that narrower fused subtract/select steps and one physical divider\nreduce the critical arithmetic delay and routing congestion enough to\nexceed the 4.6 per\n…[26340 of 29412 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b32717c2f133dcb0]…\n bracketed cycles, canonical CRCs,\nthe required UART validation literal and no out-of-bounds accesses.\nCombining this measured throughput with median Fmax gives probe\nfitness 156.93, approximately 13.19 percent above the champion.\nFull formal was not run during hypothesis generation; implementation-\nphase correctness and fitness gates remain authoritative. The expected\ngain is thirteen percent with unchanged CoreMark cycles. Risks are\nincorrect next-stage tag qualification, lost held WB forwarding,\nand the remaining MEM multiplication-recovery path. Acceptance\nrequires (Fmax_new / 58.252) * (4,201,709 / cycles_new) > 1.046.\n\nNOTES: \nPATH: {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/u_mul_exact/mul_ss_63_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -10.776, 'arrival_ns': 21.071, 'logic_cells': 33, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem/u_mul_exact', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhyp-20261005-003-r5s2 | predictor | Narrow right-shift value prediction with exact MEM validation | regression | fitness=140.07 fmax=59.885 cycles=4275479\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "compl