{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_50", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r7s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261005-001-r7s0\ntitle: \\\"Predecode WB source type into four-way registered forwarding\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 178.53 at 75.013 MHz and 4,201,709 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. Its worst path starts at a MEM/WB result and crosses\n  EX forwarding and the narrow multiplication predictor. The current\n  far bypass first selects load data versus an ALU/exact-product result\n  in WB, then passes through EX's three-way operand selector. Removing\n  this serial selection can shorten multiplication, branch and address\n  paths together. LESSONS.md is absent; prior micro_opt entries and the\n  recent registered-recovery and operand-certificate results in\n  experiments/log.jsonl were reviewed. Registered bypass decisions\n  already align with ID/EX, making source-type predecode a small local\n  extension of the successful operand-preparation implementation.\nhypothesis: |\n  Expand each existing registered one-hot forwarding decision from\n  three sources to four: 0001=captured ID data, 0010=EX/MEM ALU result,\n  0100=MEM/WB ALU/exact-product result, 1000=MEM/WB extended load data.\n  Compute the far writer match in ID exactly as today, including the\n  valid, post-trap writer qualification, nonzero destination and near\n  writer priority. Split that far match using the CURRENT MEM writer's\n  EX/MEM ctrl.mem_to_reg, because that writer advances into MEM/WB on\n  the same edge that captures these forwarding selections and ID/EX.\n  Do not use next-cycle WB control combinationally to select EX data.\n  Capture, retain and clear all four bits with the existing forwarding\n  register's reset/flush/hold priority; exactly one bit must be set.\n\n  Wire MEM/WB.alu_result and MEM/WB.read_data separately to EX rather\n  than feeding the WB write-data mux into the far operand candidate.\n  Select architectural rs1/rs2 as the OR of four mutually exclusive\n  masked sources. Apply the same four-way selection to ID-prepared ALU\n  operands: AUIPC suppresses every rs1 bypass and immediate operations\n  suppress every rs2 bypass, while architectural source forwarding\n  remains independent for stores, branches, JALR and RVFI. A four-way\n  masked selection can map as two parallel two-source LUT terms and\n  one final OR, replacing the serial WB mux followed by forwarding.\n\n  Keep WB's existing load-versus-ALU mux for register-file writes and\n  RVFI. Keep both original MEM/WB data fields and their retained values\n  when dmem stalls clear WB valid. The held far-load selection must\n  continue reading retained read_data even after the older load retires;\n  never gate forwarding data by current WB valid or reg_write. Preserve\n  the MEM bypass qualification for misaligned loads and multiply repair,\n  load-use bubbles, near-over-far priority, x0 rules, divider operand\n  snapshots/cancellation and every existing flush or bus hold.\n\n  This is a micro_opt of the existing bypass mux: no new prediction\n  policy, multiplier arithmetic, recovery timing, instruction latency,\n  memory operation, pipeline stage or retirement width. Preserve the\n  exact real and ALTOPS arithmetic, decoded legality, branch training,\n  top-level ports, nret=1, RVFI fields/order and all correctness gates.\n  Source values and cycle behavior should remain identical for arbitrary\n  programs and ready sequences; the change targets physical selection\n  depth, particularly the path into the speculative multiplier.\n\n  Expect unchanged 4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles and approximately\n  eight percent better median Fmax/fitness. Extra selector flops and\n  routing of a fourth data candidate may limit the benefit. Confirm\n  source-class alignment under stalls and repairs with the existing\n  pipeline/divider suites, then run unchanged formal and canonical\n  stalled CoreMark CRC validation. Acceptance requires\n  (Fmax_new/75.013)*(4201709/cycles_new)>1.046; at unchanged cycles,\n  median Fmax must exceed 78.463598 MHz and fitness 186.74238.\n  The frequency gain is an estimate pending the timing probe.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: |\n      Add the current qualified MEM writer's mem_to_reg input and expand\n      rs1/rs2 selectors to four one-hot bits. Split the original far\n      match into WB-ALU and WB-load candidates before registering it.\n      Keep near priority, x0 exclusion, default captured-data selection\n      and exact reset/flush/hold behavior.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Widen the internal bypass selection wires and connect EX/MEM's\n      mem_to_reg to forwarding predecode. Feed MEM/WB.alu_result and\n      MEM/WB.read_data directly into separate internal EX data inputs.\n      Keep wb_w_data connected to register-file writes and RVFI, and\n      preserve every external port and all existing pipeline controls.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Accept four-way selectors and separate far ALU/load candidates.\n      Flatten rs1/rs2 forwarding into four masked terms; use the same\n      direct candidates in the prepared ALU operand network with its\n      existing AUIPC/immediate suppression. Preserve all arithmetic,\n      multiplier predictions, store sources, RVFI source snapshots,\n      branch/trap behavior and divider transactions.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update selector expectations to distinguish far ALU=4 and far\n      load=8 while retaining one-hot, priority, stability and every\n      architectural assertion. Exercise both source types on either\n      operand, near/far conflicts, x0, AUIPC/immediate raw-field aliases,\n      load-to-multiply/branch/store dependencies, load-use bubbles,\n      retained load forwarding across repeated dmem holds, and repair.\n  - file: test/test_ex_divider.py\n    description: |\n      Drive the separate far ALU/load inputs and four-bit selectors in\n      existing transaction tests. Retain all exact result, once-only\n      capture, downstream-hold, completion and cancellation assertions;\n      cover divider operands sourced from each WB candidate and fresh\n      replay after older multiply repair.\n''')\nimport json,yaml,jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Revised forwarding hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
