{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r7s0',\n'title':'Isolate memory address generation after registered multiply recovery',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 178.53 at 75.013 MHz and 4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst path starts at a MEM/WB value, crosses EX forwarding and the narrow multiply predictor, and ends at data memory. MEM currently uses the general EX/MEM alu_result as the data-bus address even though loads and stores only need rs1+imm. A dedicated address path removes multiply and general result selection from this memory-facing cone. LESSONS.md is absent; prior micro_opt entries and recent outcomes in experiments/log.jsonl were reviewed. The earlier r4s0 address specialization regressed because its newly exposed full-product recovery path still crossed MEM and EX combinationally. The present champion has registered that recovery, making this specific earlier limitation materially different.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add a dedicated effective_addr field to the existing EX/MEM payload. In EX, compute it using one combinational adder on the fully forwarded architectural rs1 and decoded immediate. Capture rs1+imm directly, bypassing AUIPC/ALU-source selection, ALU operation selection, speculative multiplication selection, and jump-link selection. Do not gate this field with additional memory-op decode on its timed input path. Capture, hold, reset and squash it with the same instruction as the existing EX/MEM fields, without adding a pipeline stage or changing any instruction latency.\n\nIn MEM, use only this registered effective_addr for io_dmemAddr, byte-lane masks, load extraction, memory alignment checks, and aligned RVFI memory addresses. Keep alu_result for the ordinary result/near-bypass path and exact-product-versus-prediction validation. Keep the existing rs2 store-data path, load extension and writeback, registered multiply repair/quarantine, divider cancellation, and branch/jump behavior. A waiting active request must remain stable for any length of dmem stall. Inactive bus addresses may differ; every accepted memory transaction and architectural RVFI value must remain identical.\n\nRetain the existing divider snapshot/consume mechanism, including the address field in its whole-payload capture as in the measured probe. Do not add unmeasured clock enables, strip divider payload bits, change the multiplier, or combine this hypothesis with writeback/forwarding refactors. Preserve real and ALTOPS arithmetic, decoder legality and trap suppression, prediction/training, near-over-far priority, x0, frontend recovery priority, nret=1, all top-level ports and every evaluation check. This is one local micro_opt: specialize an existing combinational function and its destination register field.\n\nAn isolated implementation of exactly this address specialization completed the unchanged Gowin placement options at 74.410, 79.208 and 79.208 MHz, giving a median 79.208 MHz, 5.59 percent above the champion. Placement option zero uses 3,910 logic cells, 1,067 registers, 40 LUT-RAM units, four BSRAMs and six DSPs. Its worst path is now 18.733 ns through WB, EX and conditional recovery/training, with no multiply predictor on that path. The existing complete pipeline, memory-repair and EX-divider runners pass after updating only packed-field layouts and standalone input addresses to match the added payload field. All architectural, exact-result, ordering, hold, recovery and cancellation assertions are retained.\n\nThe unchanged stalled CoreMark validation is pending. Expect unchanged measured cycles because control and arithmetic results are unchanged. At 4,201,709 cycles the measured median Fmax projects to fitness 188.514, exceeding the 186.74238 acceptance floor. Require (Fmax_new/75.013)*(4201709/cycles_new)>1.046, canonical CRCs, the UART validation literal, bounded accesses, and unchanged formal gates. Added address storage and the newly exposed branch/forwarding control path are the principal limits. These are isolated probe measurements; implementation-phase correctness and median timing remain authoritative.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'medium'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Add a 32-bit effective_addr field to ex_mem_t, adjacent to alu_result. Leave control encodings, all other payload fields and the MEM/WB/RVFI contract unchanged.'},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Compute effective_addr from fully forwarded rs1 plus in.imm and capture it directly in exec_payload. Hold, clear and squash it with EX/MEM and retain normal whole-payload divider snapshot/consume behavior. Leave general result selection, forwarding, multiply prediction and every control decision unchanged.'},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Replace alu_result with effective_addr only for data-bus addressing, lane selection, load extraction, alignment checks and aligned RVFI memory addresses. Keep exact multiplication, mismatch comparison, general result writeback, memory enables, traps, holds and registered recovery unchanged.'},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update packed EX/MEM inspection offsets for the added address field without weakening any assertion. Preserve complete architectural and recovery coverage. Check effective addresses from both forwarding sources, negative immediates, every load/store width, misalignment suppression, stable active requests under repeated bus holds, divider draining and multiplication repair/quarantine.'},\n{'file':'test/test_ex_divider.py','description':'Update the EX/MEM field layout used to unpack divider completions. Retain exact arithmetic, source snapshots, unique emission, bus-hold and cancellation assertions; ensure the added field cannot create memory effects for divider payloads.'},\n{'file':'test/test_mem_repair.py','description':'Update standalone EX/MEM packing to include effective_addr and supply it for younger memory operations. Retain every qualification, target, held-payload, quarantine and exact-product assertion; use differing alu_result and effective_addr values to verify memory ports and alignment use only the dedicated address.'}\n]}\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r7s0.yaml')\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef rep(dumper,value): return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(h,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=100))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final address-generation hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nprint('Projected fitness:',10*79.208e6/4201709,'delta_pct:',(79.208/75.013-1)*100)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
