{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_46", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r8s0.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261005-001-r8s0\ntitle: \\\"Select final writeback data before the MEM/WB register\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 188.51 at 79.208 MHz with 4,201,709 measured\n  CoreMark cycles. Its 18.733 ns worst path starts at MEM/WB load data\n  and traverses WB selection, EX forwarding and branch resolution into\n  the IF direction table. The WB stage currently selects registered\n  load versus ALU data with a 32-bit combinational mux on the far bypass\n  and register-file write paths. Moving this selection before the\n  existing MEM/WB boundary can remove one layer of logic and associated\n  control fanout from late operand delivery. LESSONS.md is absent; the\n  micro_opt history and recent outcomes were reviewed. No prior attempt\n  directly preselected final architectural writeback data in MEM.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 32-bit writeback_data field to mem_wb_t. On every ordinary MEM\n  advance capture the final architectural result directly into this\n  field: in.ctrl.mem_to_reg selects the existing sign/zero-extended\n  load_data; otherwise select the existing exact_product for a MUL-family\n  operation or in.alu_result for every other operation. This is the\n  exact composition of today's MEM exact-product selection and WB\n  load-versus-result selection, moved across the existing register\n  boundary. Retain existing read_data and alu_result fields initially\n  so payload-dependent verification can adapt without removing coverage;\n  synthesis may prune fields that no longer feed live outputs.\n\n  Drive wb_stage.w_data directly from this registered writeback_data,\n  preserving existing write qualification and destination. The core's\n  far EX forwarding and register-file write-first bypass therefore see\n  the same value on the same cycle without a WB-stage data mux. Do not\n  add a stage, alter instruction scheduling, or gate the output data\n  with WB validity. During hold_wb, retain writeback_data with the other\n  MEM/WB data fields while clearing valid only: stalled EX operands must\n  still see the previously retired writer's value. Reset and older\n  multiply-repair quarantine clear the whole bundle as today. Exact\n  multiplication still commits its full-width result on the existing\n  retirement edge, independent of the prediction and repair decision.\n\n  Preserve all real and ALTOPS arithmetic, branch prediction/training,\n  operand forwarding priority, decoder legality, alignment traps,\n  divider capture/consume/cancel, memory requests, registered multiply\n  repair, nret=1 ports and retirement order. This is solely a local\n  retiming of the existing writeback data selection; no new predictor,\n  execution stage, memory policy or recovery mechanism is introduced.\n\n  Expect unchanged canonical stalled CoreMark cycles and an eight\n  percent increase in median Gowin Fmax and fitness. At unchanged cycles,\n  acceptance requires Fmax above 82.852 MHz and fitness above 197.18146.\n  Validate ALU, extended loads, jump links, exact multiply hits/misses\n  and division results at WB and both bypass consumers; cover data-memory\n  holds after a load, WB validity clearing, older repair, reset and x0.\n  Update packed-bundle test offsets while retaining every assertion.\n  Run unchanged formal, stalled cosimulation and canonical CoreMark\n  validation, then all vendor placement options. The main risks are\n  the MEM input mux becoming critical and another EX arithmetic path\n  limiting the gain. Measurements remain authoritative.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: |\n      Add a 32-bit writeback_data field to mem_wb_t for the MEM-selected\n      final architectural destination value. Preserve all existing\n      instruction and RVFI payload fields and all top-level interfaces.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Capture writeback_data on every existing unheld, nonquarantined\n      MEM advance as mem_to_reg ? load_data : (is_mul ? exact_product :\n      in.alu_result). Preserve it on hold_wb while clearing validity,\n      and clear it with whole-bundle reset and multiply quarantine.\n      Keep exact multiplication validation, repair timing, load extension,\n      memory outputs and every other control unchanged.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Drive w_data directly from in.writeback_data, eliminating the\n      combinational load/ALU mux. Preserve w_en and w_addr exactly;\n      do not mask w_data with valid because held far forwarding needs it.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Update MEM/WB packed-field layout for the added result field.\n      Retain existing retirement, exact arithmetic, memory-hold,\n      forwarding, alignment-trap and multiply-repair assertions.\n      Check load/ALU/multiply/divide/link writeback and WB forwarding,\n      including a cleared WB-valid cycle during downstream holds.\n  - file: test/test_mem_repair.py\n    description: |\n      Update MEM/WB bundle decoding and check that writeback_data matches\n      the existing final exact result on ordinary advances and remains\n      available during holds. Retain every quarantine, once-only\n      retirement, memory-side-effect and repair-priority assertion.\n''')\nprint('Revised hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
