{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_104", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r8s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r8s0',\n'title':'Compute branch predicates before selecting forwarded operands',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 188.51 at 79.208 MHz with 4,201,709 measured CoreMark cycles. Its 18.733 ns worst path starts at MEM/WB load data and runs through WB and EX into the IF direction table. Other recent worst paths start at the registered forwarding tags and reach the same training or recovery controls. Branch resolution currently selects two complete 32-bit operands before comparing them, placing the forwarding networks in series with relation generation. LESSONS.md is absent; the micro_opt history and recent outcomes were reviewed. This proposal targets that operand-selection-to-predicate chain with an exact combinational restructuring.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Compute conditional-branch equality and ordering before selecting the forwarded operand pair. The existing candidates for rs1 are captured in.rs1_val, registered fwd_ex_mem and fwd_mem_wb; the rs2 candidates are in.rs2_val and those same two bypass values. For each of the nine candidate pairs, compute equality and unsigned less-than in parallel. Convert unsigned to signed less-than exactly using unsigned_less XOR (a[31] XOR b[31]); use the signed result only for BLT/BGE. Select each pair's relation flags with fwd_rs1_sel[i] AND fwd_rs2_sel[j], then OR the selected one-bit flags. The registered one-hot tags and near-over-far priority are unchanged. Identical-source pairs have constant equal=true and less=false; synthesis can share equalities and eliminate these redundant cases.\n\nDecode the selected relation into BEQ/BNE/BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU, inverting only for the complementary condition. Preserve default false for reserved branch_op values 2 and 3. Keep the existing 32-bit architectural source forwarding for ALU inputs, memory addresses, stores, JALR, multiplier/divider operands and RVFI. Change only how the conditional-branch predicate is computed. Keep branch_taken qualification, target alignment traps, redirect logic and timing, predictor training enable and data, all fetch behavior, registered multiply repair priority and divider cancellation exactly as today. Do not add any register, interlock, speculative result or prediction policy.\n\nThe expected gain is eight percent in Fmax and fitness with identical CoreMark cycles. The intended timing benefit is that late forwarding tags select scalar predicates instead of driving wide operand muxes ahead of comparison; bypass data also enters comparisons directly. This trades some comparator logic and routing area for a shorter serial path. Preserve all top-level nret=1 ports, exact and ALTOPS arithmetic, legality defaults, memory handshakes and retirement ordering. Existing zero-bubble and recovery assertions remain required.\n\nValidate every branch condition with all nine forwarding-source combinations, signed extremes, equal operands, unsigned wraparound, and differing signs. Cover simultaneous writes to the same register, near-over-far priority, x0, held far-load data during dmem stalls, misaligned targets and multiply repair. Use full pipeline assertions and unchanged formal, stalled cosimulation and canonical CoreMark validation. Assess all three Gowin placement options; at unchanged cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above 82.852 MHz and fitness above 197.18146. Extra comparator routing, the WB data mux or JALR path becoming critical, and synthesis refactoring the logic back to operand selection are the principal risks. This remains a hypothesis until vendor timing and correctness gates substantiate the gain.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Replace only conditional branch_cond generation with parallel relation flags for the three-by-three existing forwarding candidate pairs and scalar one-hot selection. Share unsigned ordering with signed ordering via exact sign-bit correction; retain all six branch conditions and reserved-case defaults. Preserve architectural source muxes and every downstream branch, training, recovery, divider and memory control unchanged. No new pipeline state or top-level ports.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing pipeline assertion and add branch cases covering all nine near/far/captured source combinations, all six branch operations, signed/unsigned boundary vectors, equal-source cases and same-register writer priority. Exercise WB load forwarding while WB validity clears during a downstream hold, x0, target misalignment, and older multiply repair. Check exact direction, next PC, original RVFI operands, training count and order, and absence of wrong-path memory effects.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Branch predicate hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
