18146. Validate all eight saturating transitions, consecutive same/different-index events, aliases, simultaneous prediction and training, disabled training, pending commit with no replacement, reset with a pending event, frontend holds and recovery. Compare the effective predictor to the unchanged reference state on every cycle. Run unchanged formal, stalled cosimulation, canonical CoreMark validation and all vendor placement options before claiming a gain.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'''Add the nine-bit pending-update record and update the backing direction table only from the previous registered record. Bypass the record's high bit to a matching prediction read and both bits to matching training-state reads. Capture the exact saturated successor on the original EX-training edge, allow simultaneous old commit/new capture, and clear pending validity when no replacement arrives. Preserve weakly-taken table reset, reset priority, pre-edge prediction semantics, existing ports and all fetch targets/acceptance/redirect behavior.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_fetch_predictor.py','description':'''Retain all existing prediction, reset, aliasing and same-edge assertions. Add deterministic mixed training/read sequences against a 64-entry integer saturating reference with all eight transitions; include consecutive same-index and different-index updates, prediction aliases, disabled training and reset coincident with a pending write. Check predictions before and after each edge and ensure an accepted fetch uses the pre-edge prediction.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain all existing predictor scoreboard, training qualification/order, forwarding, memory hold, divider, exact arithmetic and recovery assertions. Add tightly spaced branches sharing an index, back-to-back differing-index training and recovery while a pending event exists. Check identical fetch acceptance, next PCs, branch directions and training counts with no wrong-path side effects or lost events.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Pending-update hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Pending-update hypothesis written and schema-valid\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
