{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_122", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-001-r8s0.yaml')\nh={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-001-r8s0',\n'title':'Remove redundant outcome qualification from predictor training data',\n'category':'micro_opt',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 188.51 at 79.208 MHz with 4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its 18.733 ns worst path starts at MEM/WB load data and traverses WB forwarding and EX branch resolution into the IF direction table. The training data is actual_taken, which repeats validity, branch-kind, legality and misalignment qualification already enforced by branch_train_en. This puts extra logic and shared recovery fanout after the late comparator. LESSONS.md is absent; the prior micro_opt attempts and recent outcomes were reviewed. Larger local rewrites exposed other critical paths without exceeding the acceptance threshold; a minimal exact data-path factorization is preferable here.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Drive branch_train_taken directly from branch_cond instead of actual_taken. Keep branch_train_en and the complete direction-table update logic unchanged. The existing training enable requires a valid advancing legal conditional branch, an aligned branch target, no downstream stall, no older multiply repair, and no divider wait. Whenever that enable is true, branch_taken equals branch_cond and misalign_fault is false, so actual_taken equals branch_cond. When enable is false, the table performs no update and the value of training data has no effect. This is an exact don't-care optimization of an internal qualified data signal, not a weaker validation or a new prediction policy.\n\nPreserve actual_taken for redirects and every other existing consumer. Preserve branch_cond's signed/unsigned comparisons and reserved defaults, branch_taken qualification, jump/branch alignment traps, predictor indexing/reset/saturation and update edge, fetch acceptance, older repair priority and all RVFI values. Do not remove any gate from branch_train_en or alter target, redirect, squash or memory logic. No added state, stage, queue, replay, or policy change is needed. Keep nret=1, top-level ports, decoder legality defaults, exact and ALTOPS arithmetic, divider transactions and memory handshakes unchanged.\n\nThe intended benefit is to send the comparator's result directly to the counter update without routing it through branch_taken and recovery/alignment qualification. That removes serial logic and isolates counter data from recovery fanout while leaving the qualifying enable intact. Expect a six percent gain in Fmax and fitness with identical 4,201,709 measured CoreMark cycles. At unchanged cycles acceptance requires median Fmax above 82.852 MHz and fitness above 197.18146. The main risks are vendor optimization already recognizing the qualification redundancy and another execute or writeback path limiting the gain.\n\nRetain all pipeline scoreboard and architectural checks. For every enabled event require the new training data to equal the original architectural branch outcome; disabled events must leave the table unchanged regardless of comparator value. Exercise all branch conditions, aligned and misaligned targets, legal/reserved instructions, stalls, older multiply repair, x0, and near/far forwarding including retained WB load data. Verify the predictor's complete sequence of counter updates, predictions, accepted fetch PCs and retirement order remains unchanged. Run unchanged formal, stalled cosimulation, canonical CoreMark validation and all three Gowin placements before claiming improvement.''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':6,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Change only branch_train_taken to the raw branch_cond. Document that unchanged branch_train_en implies valid legal aligned advancing conditional-branch execution, making branch_cond identical to actual_taken on every training edge. Keep actual_taken and all of its recovery consumers, the enable logic, architectural comparator and all stage state unchanged.'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every existing predictor reference-state, training qualification/order, recovery, hold, forwarding, arithmetic and RVFI assertion. Add enabled-event equivalence checks and disabled-event cases with both comparator outcomes, including misaligned branches, imem/dmem stalls and older multiply repair. Check no counter update occurs without the unchanged training enable and predictions/fetch acceptance remain cycle-identical. Do not require a particular inactive training-data value.'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(h,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(h,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Minimal training-data hypothesis written and schema-valid')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
