{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n print(d['id'],d.get('category'),d.get('outcome'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('fmax_mhz'),d.get('cycles'),d['title'])\n if d.get('category')=='structural':\n  h=d.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print('PROPOSAL:',h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('PATH:',d.get('critical_path'))\n  print('NOTES:',d.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-df5bec5 micro_opt improvement 12.12 5.442 4491485 Baseline retest for cores/bench\nhyp-20261005-001-r1s0 micro_opt regression 13.11 5.888 4491485 Share and width-prune the combinational DIV/REM datapath\nhyp-20261005-002-r1s1 structural improvement 104.51 46.944 4491817 Remove the combinational divide chain with a shared iterative divider\nPROPOSAL: Replace only the real-hardware DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one\nclocked radix-2 restoring divider, shared across all four operations.\nCapture the fully forwarded operands and operation exactly once when a\nvalid division instruction can start. Use registered divisor, quotient,\nand 33-bit partial remainder; execute one trial subtraction and quotient\nbit per cycle for 32 iterations. Register signed-magnitude preparation\nand final sign correction separately so neither forms a long chain with\nthe iterative subtractor. Quotient sign is the operand-sign XOR, while\nremainder sign follows the dividend. Handle zero divisor and signed\nINT_MIN/-1 explicitly with the existing RV32M bit results. Eliminate all\nsynthesizable division and modulo operators from the real ALU branch.\nKeep base integer operations and the existing multiplier implementation\non their current single-cycle path; this is one change in the structure\nof division execution, with no predictor or memory re