red divisor, quotient,\nand 33-bit partial remainder; execute one trial subtraction and quotient\nbit per cycle for 32 iterations. Register signed-magnitude preparation\nand final sign correction separately so neither forms a long chain with\nthe iterative subtractor. Quotient sign is the operand-sign XOR, while\nremainder sign follows the dividend. Handle zero divisor and signed\nINT_MIN/-1 explicitly with the existing RV32M bit results. Eliminate all\nsynthesizable division and modulo operators from the real ALU branch.\nKeep base integer operations and the existing multiplier implementation\non their current single-cycle path; this is one change in the structure\nof division execution, with no predictor or memory redesign.\n\nGive \n…[37681 of 40753 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:76a11ae0fa8e477c]…\nompletion-control or\nfrontend fanout from its data or comparison results.\n\nFor MULHSU and MULH, derive the exact signed high word from the registered\nunsigned product using high_signed = high_unsigned - (a[31] ? b : 0)\nfor MULHSU, and a further subtraction of (b[31] ? a : 0) for MULH.\nPut each correction subtraction on its own registered step, rather\nthan chaining corrections after the multiplier or in the OC bypass.\nThe held OC/EX sources supply original full-width a and b throughout.\nMUL and MULHU skip correction states. Preserve all RV32M exceptional\ncases and exact modulo-32-bit results. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS use the\nexisting exact four fo\n notes: \nhyp-20261005-003-r13s2 predictor regression 194.83 82.089 4213444 Predict relational branch conditions with 8-bit comparison and registered exact repair\n path: {'from': 'cpu/u_oc/reg_q.ctrl.alu_op_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_oc/reg_q.rs1_val_5_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.011, 'arrival_ns': 17.305, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_oc']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
