{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'structural|hyp-20261005-003-r2s2|hyp-20261005-002-r2s1|multiply|multiplier|pipeline' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share and width-prune the combinational DIV/REM datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the four real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with one shared unsigned\\nmagnitude divider that produces quotient and remainder together. Implement\\nan explicitly unrolled radix-2 restoring recurrence with compile-time\\nwidths: step k consumes the next dividend bit, has a k-bit candidate\\nremainder, and subtracts only divisor[k-1:0] using a k+1-bit difference.\\nAccept that subtraction only when its borrow is clear and every omitted\\nupper divisor bit is zero. Thus the subtractors grow from 1 to 32 bits,\\nrather than carrying full-width arithmetic through every step. Use the\\nsubtraction's borrow to select the new remainder and emit the quotient\\nbit, avoiding a separat\n…[59954 of 63026 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5156041a46c15d73]…\nor\\nimem/dmem stalls. Verify deterministic reset, single training under\\nholds, prediction/instruction pairing, no wrong-path stores, actual\\nRVFI successor and monotonic order, bubble-free correct predictions,\\nand divider dependencies/completion with predicted control transfers.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 117.75, \"delta_pct\": 12.67, \"vs_baseline\": 871.53, \"fmax_mhz\": 49.474, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201709, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3000, \"ff\": 841, \"seeds\": [50.61, 49.474, 49.474], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.61, 12], [1, 49.474, 14], [2, 49.474, 14]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.759, \"arrival_ns\": 25.054, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T00:53:18.497577Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 2}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
