, 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if']}}\nPROPOSAL: {'motivation': 'The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns worst path containing 156 cells through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts or\\nrecorded lessons for this core. The four combinational division/remainder\\noperators in alu.sv are the strongest candidate for this exceptionally\\ndeep arithmetic cone. Even infrequent DIV/REM instructions place that\\nhardware on the shared execute-result path and constrain the clock used\\nby every instruction. Serializing division should substantially raise\\nFmax and reduce LUT pressure, provided its a\n…[13844 of 16916 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1271d4b0e08c2bde]…\nequests, correct JAL/JALR link and target,\\nunique monotonic RVFI orders, correct operand/pc_next records and\\neventual target retirement. Cover an older stalled memory operation\\nahead of the branch, imem stalls during recovery, consecutive taken\\ntransfers, load-to-branch forwarding, not-taken branches, reserved\\nencodings and misaligned targets. Check one extra recovery cycle\\nwith always-ready buses and unchanged straight-line issue rate;\\nretain every existing trap, arithmetic and backpressure assertion.\\n'}]}\nNOTES: \n{'id': 'hyp-20261005-003-r2s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'title': 'Instruction-qualified bimodal prediction with one-bit branch recovery', 'outcome': 'improvement', 'fitness': 117.75, 'fmax_mhz': 49.474, 'cycles': 4201709, 'dsp': 6, 'lutram': 8, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.759, 'arrival_ns': 25.054, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}}\nLESSONS exists: False\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
