{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_13", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg --files --hidden -g '*coremark*' -g '*sta*' -g '*.rpt' -g '\"'!formal/riscv-formal/**'\"' -g '\"'!cores/*/rtl/**'\"'; sed -n '1,220p' test/cosim/reference.py; sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/test/test_alu.py; sed -n '1,110p' cores/bench/test/test_ex_divider.py\"", "aggregated_output": "bench/programs/coremark/coremark.h\nbench/programs/coremark/coremark.md5\nfpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\nbench/programs/coremark/core_state.c\ntools/agents/test_static_agent.py\ntools/agents/static_agent.py\nbench/programs/coremark/docs/coremark_profile_o0_joined.png\ntools/eval/test_bench_stall_gen.py\nbench/programs/coremark/docs/html/files/coremark-h.html\nbench/programs/coremark/docs/html/files/docs/core_state.png\nbench/programs/coremark/docs/html/files/core_state-c.html\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"RV32IM reference interpreter for the cosim. Mirrors the DUT's trap\ndiscipline so cosim traces stay aligned across illegal / misaligned\nencodings.\n\nTrap policy (matches rtl/decoder.sv default-illegal + rtl/ex_stage.sv +\nrtl/mem_stage.sv misalign traps):\n\n  - Reserved R-type:        funct7=0x20 with fn3 ∈ {1,2,3,4,6,7}\n  - Reserved OP-IMM shifts: SLLI/SRLI/SRAI with disallowed funct7\n  - Reserved LOAD funct3:   3, 6, 7\n  - Reserved STORE funct3:  3..7\n  - Reserved BRANCH funct3: 2, 3\n  - JALR funct3 != 0\n  - Non-EBREAK SYSTEM:      ECALL, CSR ops, MRET, …\n  - Unknown opcode (AMO etc.)\n  - Misaligned LH/LHU/LW/SH/SW\n  - Misaligned BRANCH (taken) / JAL / JALR target\n\nOn trap the retirement is reported with rvfi_trap=1, rd_addr=0,\nrd_wdata=0, mem_*=0, npc=pc+4. The DUT's mem_stage / ex_stage match\nthis on the same encodings.\n\nModifications to this file require explicit user approval.\"\"\"\nimport struct, sys\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nXLEN = 32\nMASK = (1 << XLEN) - 1\nMEM_BYTES = 1 << 20  # 1 MiB\n\n# MMIO UART. Write