specialization removes the general ALU result selection from\nmemory addressing; other forwarding or control paths may limit gains.\n\n[{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add a 32-bit effective_addr field to ex_mem_t, preserving every\\nexisting control, source operand, instruction and RVFI field.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Compute effective_addr directly from fully forwarded rs1 plus\\nin.imm and capture it in the existing EX/MEM payload, independently\\nof the general ALU and jump/product result selection. Preserve all\\nholds, bubbles, divider snapshots and older multiplication squashes.\\n'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Replace memory-address uses of in.alu_result with in.effective_addr\\nfor active bus addresses, alignment faults, byte masks, load lane\\nextraction and RVFI aligned addresses. Keep multiplication validation,\\nforwarding results, store data, writeback and held-WB behavior intact.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Adjust packed EX/MEM metadata extraction for the added field while\\nretaining all assertions. Cover forwarded ALU/load/multiply bases,\\npositive and negative offsets, byte/half/word lanes, alignment traps,\\ndata-memory holds and multiply repair followed by a memory operation.\\nCheck exact active addresses, stable stalled requests, masks, data,\\noriginal RVFI operands and single monotonic retirement.\\n'}, {'file': 'test/test_ex_divider.py', 'description': 'Update the packed EX/MEM field layout for effective_addr without\\nweakening any divider completion, forwarding, hold or consume check.\\n'}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
