{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"agent_message","text":"The eight-entry probe saved 5.37% of CoreMark cycles, but timing exposed a long redirect-to-queue control path. I’m refining the hypothesis to make queue capacity depend only on registered occupancy and to clear entries on the redirect edge using the existing ID flush priority. This removes that feedback path; the refinement is unmeasured."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_86", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml, json, jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-002-r7s1.yaml');d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text())\nd['title']='Decouple fetch with an eight-entry queue and registered capacity'\nh=d['hypothesis']\nh=h.replace('Permit enqueue on a full queue only when a dequeue occurs on the same edge. For simultaneous full dequeue/enqueue, the pre-edge head instruction is consumed and the replacement is written at the old tail, with both pointers advancing and occupancy unchanged.', 'Drive fetch space exclusively from registered occupancy < 8; do not feed dequeue or redirect combinationally into this capacity signal. A full queue may dequeue, but cannot accept a replacement until the following cycle shows space. When occupancy is between one and seven, simultaneous enqueue/dequeue advances both pointers and leaves count unchanged. This intentionally breaks the backend-to-fetch ready path at registered occupancy.')\nh=h.replace('Empty entries are never valid;', 'Only occupied entries or a ready empty pass-through instruction are valid;')\nh=h.replace('but empty/cleared output validity must gate all instruction effects;', 'but stored payload cannot produce a valid instruction after the clearing edge;')\nh=h.replace('validity qualified by io_imemReady and \"'!redirect'\"', 'validity qualified by io_imemReady')\nh=h.replace('and prevent cleared head validity from creating a younger capture.', 'and rely on the existing highest-priority ID flush to prevent a younger capture. Present head validity from occupancy or raw-ready empty pass-through only, without a combinational \"'!redirect term. On the redirect edge, clear FIFO metadata and ID/EX together. Keep redirect gating on fetch enqueue, but do not propagate it into the FIFO data/valid lookup or capacity network.'\"')\nh += '''\\\\n\\\\nAn isolated eight-entry empty-pass-through probe with flat payload storage passed all eight ready/stalled selftest and random-program full-trace comparisons against the unchanged ISS. Unchanged run_coremark_ipc completed ten iterations in 3,975,958 bracketed cycles, 5.37 percent fewer than 4,201,709, with all canonical CRCs, the required validation literal and no out-of-bounds accesses. However, the preliminary queue returned capacity combinationally from dequeue and masked head validity with redirect. Its median vendor Fmax was only 67.487 MHz; a reported 20-cell path ran from WB result selection through EX recovery into ID forwarding selection. That preliminary circuit is a regression, not acceptance evidence. This final hypothesis removes those two queue-control feedback paths using registered capacity and ID's existing flush priority. That refinement has not been timed or fully proven. At the measured cycle count, acceptance needs median Fmax above approximately 74.244 MHz. Early unchanged formal checks passed causal, backward PC, illegal, unique and liveness properties on the preliminary flat-storage probe; complete formal and the cover check remain required implementation-phase gates. No formal result from the earlier packed-struct-array probe counts as a pass: it failed reachability because Yosys discarded the payload.''' \nd['hypothesis']=h\nd['changes'][0]['description']='Add an eight-entry elastic circular FIFO carrying full if_id_t payloads as flat packed bits. Use three-bit head/tail pointers, four-bit registered occupancy, and fetch-space = count < 8 with no pop/redirect combinational feedback. Allow empty pass-through qualified by raw bus readiness and simultaneous enqueue/dequeue when not full. A full dequeue frees capacity on the next cycle. Head validity depends only on occupancy or raw readiness; existing ID flush prevents redirect-cycle capture while FIFO pointers/count clear synchronously. Preserve all packed payload bits, ordering, capacity and prediction/PC pairing.'\nd['changes'][1]['description'] += ' Keep FIFO head validity independent of redirect; flush_id clears ID/EX before any capture, while redirect synchronously clears the FIFO and suppresses enqueue. Do not add dequeue-to-fetch-space combinational feedback.'\nd['changes'][4]['description']='Add directed queue tests for empty pass-through, independent producer/consumer stalls, full dequeue with replacement accepted on the next cycle, nonfull simultaneous push/pop, wraparound, capacity/count invariants, order and prediction/PC pairing. Exercise reset/redirect with pending push/pop at every occupancy; after the clear edge no stored instruction remains valid, and ID flush prevents any redirect-cycle younger capture.'\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert d['id']=='hyp-20261005-002-r7s1' and d['category']=='structural'\nprint('Final hypothesis schema valid:',p)\nprint('Acceptance Fmax for preliminary cycle count:',75.013*1.046*3975958/4201709)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
