capture. Preserve current instruction-qualified predictor, training and target logic; redirect overrides enqueue and all PC holds. Raw fetched bundle carries the exact PC/instruction/direction for enqueue, while backend holds no longer prevent a ready fetch with available space.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\n    \"description\": \"Treat frontend availability as queued-head valid rather than raw bus readiness. Preserve load-use bubble and downstream hold semantics using queued source fields, and existing redirect/divider/dmem priority. Empty queue advances an invalid ID payload while older instructions drain. Do not let io_imemReady invalidate a buffered head.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_fetch_fifo.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Add directed queue tests for empty pass-through, independent producer/consumer stalls, full dequeue with replacement accepted on the next cycle, nonfull simultaneous push/pop, wraparound, capacity/count invariants, order and prediction/PC pairing. Exercise reset/redirect with pending push/pop at every occupancy; after the clear edge no stored instruction remains valid, and ID flush prevents any redirect-cycle younger capture.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n    \"description\": \"Update timing-specific frontend scoreboard to distinguish fetch enqueue from ID dequeue, with a queue of exact PC/instruction/prediction tuples. Preserve arithmetic, traps, RVFI ordering, bypass, memory holds and recovery assertions. Exercise instruction stalls while buffered work issues, filling during backend waits, load-use head retention, all control transfers and older multiply repair at varying occupancies. Check single retirement and no wrong-path memory effects or uncanceled divides; retain architectural coverage for real and ALTOPS products.\"\n  }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
