{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predictor|gshare|return.address|btb|ras|branch.predict|bimodal' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "3:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Remove the combinational divide chain with a shared iterative divider\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns worst path containing 156 cells through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts or\\nrecorded lessons for this core. The four combinational division/remainder\\noperators in alu.sv are the strongest candidate for this exceptionally\\ndeep arithmetic cone. Even infrequent DIV/REM instructions place that\\nhardware on the shared execute-result path and constrain the clock used\\nby every instruction. Serializing division should substantially raise\\nFmax and reduce LUT pressure, provided its added CoreMark cycles cost\\nless than the frequency improvement under the existing bus stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: fitness 12.12, median Fmax\\n5.442 MHz, and a 199.837 ns worst path containing 156 cells through\\nforwarding and u_ex/u_alu. There are no prior structural attempts or\\nrecorded lessons for this core. The four combinational division/remainder\\noperators in alu.sv are the strongest candidate for this exceptionally\\ndeep arithmetic cone. Even infrequent DIV/REM instructions place that\\nhardware on the shared execute-result path and constrain the clock used\\nby every instruction. Serializing division should substantially raise\\nFmax and reduce LUT pressure, provided its added CoreMark cycles cost\\nless than the frequency improvement under the existing bus stalls.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace only the real-hardware DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU datapaths with one\\nclocked radix-2 restoring divider, shared across all four operations.\\nCapture the fully forwarded operands and operation exactly once when a\\nvalid division instruction can start. Use registered divisor, quotient,\\nand 33-bit partial remainder; execute one trial subtraction and quotient\\nbit per cycle for 32 iterations. Register sign\n…[307812 of 310884 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c67afc1b4e1f64b6]…\nB failures followed by dependent\\nALU/load/store/branch/JALR/DIV/REM work, independent bus stalls,\\nretained sources and older multiply repair. Verify exact addresses,\\noriginal operands, correct single retirement and no wrong-path\\nmemory effects. Adjust packed-bundle offsets only where required.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 194.39, \"delta_pct\": -10.54, \"vs_baseline\": 1503.88, \"fmax_mhz\": 84.2, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4331530, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4462, \"ff\": 1461, \"seeds\": [75.138, 84.2, 84.2], \"perturbations\": [[0, 75.138, 12], [1, 84.2, 9], [2, 84.2, 9]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_oc/reg_q.rs2_val_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s95\", \"slack_ns\": -8.309, \"arrival_ns\": 18.603, \"logic_cells\": 37, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T06:53:36.773476Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
