{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_32", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r11s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Reduce conditional-branch interference with a compact gshare predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion uses only 64 untagged bimodal counters indexed by PC[7:2].\n  This aliases branches throughout CoreMark and cannot distinguish outcomes\n  correlated with preceding branches. The successful r2 predictor kept\n  recovery to one direction bit; the r8 successor-validation experiment\n  regressed after adding later recovery and wide target checks. Improve\n  direction accuracy while preserving the present EX recovery stage and\n  exact instruction-derived direct targets. LESSONS.md is absent; the\n  predictor-category experiment history was reviewed.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the 64-entry bimodal direction table with one 256-entry gshare\n  table of two-bit saturating counters and an eight-bit resolved conditional\n  history register. Compute its fetch index as PC[9:2] XOR history, and\n  capture that exact index with each accepted instruction through IF/ID,\n  ID/OC and OC/EX. Train the captured index exactly once when the original\n  legal aligned conditional branch advances through EX; never recompute\n  its index from a subsequently changed history. Update the current counter\n  at that index rather than a stale captured counter. Reset counters to\n  weakly taken and history to zero. Same-edge lookup sees pre-write state.\n\n  Shift only actual resolved branch outcomes into history, on the same\n  existing branch_train_en event. There are no speculative history updates,\n  history checkpoints, or history changes on fetch acceptance, JAL, JALR,\n  invalid instructions, holds, divider waits or older multiply recovery.\n  History is advisory predictor state; EX may update it before a subsequent\n  older recovery without affecting architectural correctness. Predictor\n  training remains suppressed by the existing squash/advancement controls.\n\n  Keep legal-instruction predecode, aligned immediate branch/JAL targets,\n  exact unconditional JAL prediction and present JALR behavior unchanged.\n\n…[2046 of 5118 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:efe8a2b1ce86343a]…\n      instruction's captured lookup index. Preserve training qualification,\n      one-bit branch recovery, exact targets, arithmetic and divider logic.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Widen the internal predictor training-index wire without changing\n      any top-level port, stage control or retirement boundary.\n  - file: test/test_fetch_predictor.py\n    description: |\n      Retain legality, alignment, flush and acceptance assertions; adapt\n      explicit table-size/index expectations. Check history advances only\n      on qualified training, captured-index training despite changed\n      history, saturation, alias separation and same-edge pre-write lookup.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Adapt packed metadata extraction and preserve all architectural\n      assertions. Exercise back-to-back conditional branches, both recovery\n      directions, fetch/decode holds, dmem stalls, divider waits, older\n      multiply recovery and wrong-path memory effects with changed history.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
