{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r11s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Predict relational branches with a 16-bit operand projection and exact MEM validation\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Recent failed experiments repeatedly expose EX branch/control recovery\n  paths into fetch or decode. The champion already has registered OC/EX\n  operands and registered older multiply recovery, allowing a cheap branch\n  outcome candidate to be checked without a full comparison driving EX\n  recovery. LESSONS.md is absent and predictor history was reviewed: r8's\n  wholesale later branch resolution increased cycles, while r10 narrowed\n  arithmetic register results and still encountered EX control timing.\n  This proposal instead keeps fast EX direction recovery and predicts only\n  the four relational branch predicates. A sequential canonical CoreMark\n  profile has 529588 bracketed conditional branches, including 151852\n  relational branches; projecting the top and bottom bytes disagrees on\n  only 1623 relational outcomes. A 256-entry gshare profile did not improve\n  direction accuracy, so a larger history predictor is not the chosen angle.\nhypothesis: |\n  For BLT, BGE, BLTU and BGEU in EX, replace the full-width comparison with\n  one explicit sixteen-bit comparison of projected architectural operands:\n  projected_rs1 = {rs1[31:24], rs1[7:0]} and likewise for rs2. Signed branches\n  compare these as signed sixteen-bit values; unsigned branches compare\n  them as unsigned. Keep BEQ/BNE comparisons exact at thirty-two bits.\n  Retaining the high byte preserves the architectural sign and all ordering\n  when high bytes differ; retaining the low byte handles many small values.\n  The omitted middle bits remain arbitrary legal operand bits. This is an\n  advisory outcome prediction, never a range restriction or correctness\n  certificate. Preserve original full-width rs1/rs2 for MEM and RVFI.\n\n  Keep the existing 64-entry bimodal direction table, fetch instruction\n  qualification, immediate branch/JAL targets and JALR behavior. In EX,\n  treat the projected predicate as provi\n…[5209 of 8281 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6ae832c970b3cd4a]…\noth incorrect outcomes, check exact BEQ/BNE,\n      full source preservation, advancement-gated training and alignment\n      suppression. Distinguish provisional outcomes from retired results.\n  - file: test/test_mem_repair.py\n    description: |\n      Retain every multiply, hold, trap and quarantine assertion. Add exact\n      branch validation, success without a bubble, registered recovery in\n      both directions regardless of encoded rd bits, bubbles/illegal\n      exclusion, and exact taken versus not-taken misaligned-target traps.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve all original architectural and memory assertions. Exercise\n      both candidate errors with dependent ALU/load/store/JALR/DIV/REM,\n      independent younger stores, back-to-back branches, retained operands,\n      instruction/data stalls and older multiply recovery. Verify exact\n      next PC/trap/source snapshots, single retirement, repair priority,\n      no wrong-path memory effect and progress after cancellation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
