{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|branch|return|JALR|jalr|gshare|bimodal|RAS' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share and width-prune the combinational DIV/REM datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the four real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with one shared unsigned\\nmagnitude divider that produces quotient and remainder together. Implement\\nan explicitly unrolled radix-2 restoring recurrence with compile-time\\nwidths: step k consumes the next dividend bit, has a k-bit candidate\\nremainder, and subtracts only divisor[k-1:0] using a k+1-bit difference.\\nAccept that subtraction only when its borrow is clear and every omitted\\nupper divisor bit is zero. Thus the subtractors grow from 1 to 32 bits,\\nrather than carrying full-width arithmetic through every step. Use the\\nsubtraction's borrow to select the new remainder and emit the quotient\\nbit, avoiding a separat\n…[415359 of 418431 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d1c9cdbc1c6f1c7c]…\nrate.\\n\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"description\": \"Exercise interleaved branches with colliding low PC bits and\\ndeliberate folded-index aliases under independent bus stalls.\\nCheck exact ordered retirement, both repair directions, once-only\\ntraining and absence of wrong-path memory effects.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 195.39, \"delta_pct\": -10.08, \"vs_baseline\": 1512.13, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.938, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4193623, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4050, \"ff\": 1265, \"seeds\": [81.033, 81.938, 81.938], \"perturbations\": [[0, 81.033, 9], [1, 81.938, 12], [2, 81.938, 12]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_oc/reg_q.alu_b_val_29_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -7.341, \"arrival_ns\": 17.635, \"logic_cells\": 9, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_mem\", \"cpu/u_oc\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 9, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T08:12:41.319753Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 12}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
