{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_48", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r13s2.yaml')\np.write_text('''id: hyp-20261005-003-r13s2\ntitle: \\\"Predict relational branch conditions with 16-bit comparison and registered exact repair\\\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 217.29 at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent and predictor history was reviewed.\n  Smaller folded-PC tables, counter recoding and delayed control-flow\n  validation regressed. A return profile finds only 13,735 timed JALRs,\n  so return prediction alone has insufficient upside. Ordinary direction\n  policy improvements also save too few errors to justify larger tables.\n  The current full-width relational branch comparisons feed same-cycle\n  EX redirect, frontend flush and predictor training. A computational\n  branch-condition predictor can shorten that feedback while retaining\n  immediate EX correction of ordinary fetch-direction mistakes.\nhypothesis: |\n  Introduce one stateless computational predictor for relational branch\n  conditions. Keep BEQ and BNE exact with their existing full-width\n  equality checks. For BLTU/BGEU compare only rs1[15:0] and rs2[15:0],\n  complementing the less-than result for BGEU. For BLT/BGE use the true\n  32-bit sign bits: when rs1[31] differs from rs2[31], signed less-than\n  is rs1[31]; otherwise predict from unsigned low-16-bit less-than.\n  Complement this result for BGE. Read only registered OC/EX operands,\n  with no new forwarding or operand-range assumptions. Wider values\n  remain legal and are always checked against exact execution.\n\n  EX uses the provisional branch condition to correct the accepted fetch\n  direction immediately, using the existing direction-XOR recovery and\n  exact PC+immediate target. Qualify provisional taken with valid, legal\n  branch encoding and target alignment. Keep JAL/JALR resolution, link\n  values and alignment traps exact in EX. Preserve current EX advancement,\n  dmem/divider hold gating, older registered recovery priority and flush\n  behavior. Unlike r8s2, ordinary bimodal direction errors still recover\n  in EX; only a wrong computed relational condition needs late repair.\n\n  Capture provisional effective-taken in the existing EX/MEM branch_taken\n  field, together with original full-width architectural rs1/rs2 and the\n  existing exact branch_target. Existing bundles already carry these\n  fields, so no extra operand bank or full-width prediction target is\n  needed. EX must not declare a conditional branch illegal based on its\n  approximate condition: determine conditional target traps exactly in\n  MEM. A known misaligned target cannot be provisionally taken in EX.\n\n  In MEM recompute the architectural condition with full-width signed or\n  unsigned comparison, independently of the predictor. Actual effective\n  taken requires a legal branch, true exact condition and aligned target.\n  Set the final trap for an exactly taken misaligned conditional target;\n  its architectural successor is PC+4. For every conditional branch,\n  commit exact pc_next as actual target or PC+4, and preserve original\n  RVFI operands, instruction and retirement order. Compare actual\n  effective-taken against the captured provisional effective-taken.\n  A direction mismatch becomes a registered MEM/WB repair, ORed with\n  the existing independently qualified multiply mismatch. Capture the\n  exact branch successor in the same repair-target register. A condition\n  mismatch that leaves the effective successor unchanged needs no replay.\n\n  The validating older branch retires once with exact next-PC and trap\n  fields. On the next cycle reuse existing older recovery to redirect to\n  that exact successor, quarantine younger MEM requests even if unready,\n  squash younger EX/OC/decode and saved operands, suppress younger EX\n  redirects and cancel a younger divider or held completion. Correct\n  provisional conditions add no recovery cycle. Branches write no integer\n  destination, so exact MEM branch validation must have no combinational\n  path into OC writer eligibility, bypass data/readiness or memory bus\n  enables. Express MEM writer qualification from original control and\n  memory-alignment checks, explicitly excluding branches; apply exact\n  conditional trap state only to the registered retirement payload.\n\n  Move conditional predictor training to a registered MEM/WB event with\n  original PC[7:2] and exact actual direction. Generate it once when a\n  legal aligned branch is accepted by MEM, excluding hold_wb, invalid\n  bubbles and older recovery. Consume each registered event once in IF\n  even if the following instruction stalls. A branch's own ordinary EX\n  repair must not discard its eventual training. A pending event from a\n  valid older branch may train during younger recovery; quarantined\n  younger branches generate none. Read the then-current two-bit counter\n  when consuming the event, preserving consecutive same-index updates\n  and pre-edge fetch lookup semantics. Retain all 64 entries, PC[7:2]\n  indexing, binary saturation, weakly-taken reset and immediate JAL policy.\n\n  An architectural profile of the unchanged canonical 2K, -O3,\n  ten-iteration ELF finds 529,588 timed conditional branches. The proposed\n  sign-aware low-16 comparator disagrees on 640 outcomes, versus 5,140\n  for naive signed low-16 comparison. This is a sequential reference\n  profile, not a measured RTL cycle saving, Fmax result or correctness\n  proof. Fewer than 0.13 percent of branches require arithmetic validation\n  correction in that profile. Delayed table training and wrong-path\n  executions can change RTL behavior. The expected eight-percent fitness\n  gain has low confidence and depends on removing full-width comparison\n  from immediate recovery/training rather than improved direction accuracy.\n  Exact MEM comparison, control fanout and the existing load-to-OC path\n  remain timing risks. Require\n  (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046 for acceptance.\n\n  Preserve nret=1, all external ports, decoder default-illegal and reserved\n  encodings, SYSTEM rules, exact real/ALTOPS arithmetic, bus handshakes,\n  memory alignment and every hard invariant. Keep comparator prediction\n  active in formal builds and validate every branch with full-width\n  operands there too; add no symbolic range or outcome assumptions.\n  Run unchanged formal, meaningful directed unit tests, ready/stalled\n  trace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/MMIO/bracket/completion/bounded-access\n  checks and median vendor Gowin timing. Retain every existing architectural\n  assertion, adapting only internal layouts or prediction-specific timing\n  expectations to the explicit provisional/validation stages.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Add shared unsigned low-16 less-than and full-sign-aware signed\n      prediction for BLT/BGE/BLTU/BGEU. Keep BEQ/BNE exact, use provisional\n      effective-taken for immediate EX direction-XOR correction and the\n      existing EX/MEM branch_taken field, and defer conditional alignment\n      traps to exact MEM validation. Remove exact EX branch training while\n      preserving jump, arithmetic, bypass and divider behavior.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: |\n      Compute full-width actual branch conditions from existing registered\n      source operands. Correct branch pc_next and taken-target trap fields\n      at retirement, register direction mismatch into shared older repair,\n      and capture the exact repair target. Register once-only exact branch\n      training events. Keep validation entirely off current OC forwarding\n      and dmem control by explicit nonbranch writer qualification.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: |\n      Route registered MEM branch-training events to IF instead of EX\n      training. Preserve existing oldest-repair priority, quarantine,\n      frontend recovery, divider cancellation, single retirement boundary\n      and all top-level ports. Document that the existing older repair\n      signal now covers multiply and relational-condition validation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve exact RVFI and wrong-path-effect assertions. Add all four\n      relational branches with equal low halves and unequal high halves,\n      sign disagreement, negative operands, unsigned boundaries and both\n      mismatch directions. Cover speculative condition changes around\n      misaligned targets, exact BEQ/BNE, consecutive branches, retained\n      operands, wrong-path stores/divides, both bus stalls and older\n      multiply recovery. Check immediate ordinary direction correction,\n      once-only late repair and exact registered predictor training.\n  - file: test/test_mem_repair.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the existing registered repair tests to exact branch\n      validation, corrected successors and traps, branch-only mismatch,\n      no replay when effective successors agree, back-to-back training\n      events, MEM holds and recovery quarantine. Retain all multiply\n      validation and exact retirement coverage.\n''')\nprint(p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
