{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_66", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r13s2.yaml');s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('with 16-bit comparison','with 8-bit comparison')\ns=s.replace('rs1[15:0] and rs2[15:0]','rs1[7:0] and rs2[7:0]').replace('unsigned low-16-bit less-than','unsigned low-8-bit less-than')\ns=s.replace('  Capture provisional effective-taken in the existing EX/MEM branch_taken\\\\n  field, together with original full-width architectural rs1/rs2 and the', '  Capture the raw provisional condition, before alignment qualification,\\\\n  in the existing EX/MEM branch_taken field, together with original\\\\n  full-width architectural rs1/rs2 and the')\ns=s.replace('''  In MEM recompute the architectural condition with full-width signed or\n  unsigned comparison, independently of the predictor. Actual effective\n  taken requires a legal branch, true exact condition and aligned target.''','''  In MEM form the exact full-width condition by lexicographic validation.\n  Compare original operand upper bits [31:8]. If they are equal, the\n  captured raw low-byte condition is already exact. Otherwise compare\n  those upper 24 bits signed for BLT/BGE or unsigned for BLTU/BGEU,\n  complementing less-than for greater-or-equal. The upper comparison\n  decides the full result whenever upper bits differ. BEQ/BNE reuse\n  their captured full-width exact condition. This is exact for arbitrary\n  32-bit operands; no range certificate or prediction assumption is\n  accepted. It avoids a redundant second low-byte comparator in MEM.\n  Actual effective taken requires a legal branch, true exact condition\n  and aligned target.''')\ns=s.replace('''  effective-taken against the captured provisional effective-taken.''','''  effective-taken against captured raw provisional condition AND target\n  alignment, reconstructing the precise effective direction used in EX.''')\ns=s.replace('''  sign-aware low-16 comparator disagrees on 640 outcomes, versus 5,140\n  for naive signed low-16 comparison.''','''  full-sign-aware low-byte comparator disagrees on 4,723 outcomes when\n  BEQ/BNE remain exact, about 0.89 percent of branches.''')\ns=s.replace('''  Fewer than 0.13 percent of branches require arithmetic validation\n  correction in that profile.''','''  Only computed-condition errors require late validation recovery;\n  ordinary fetch-direction errors retain their existing EX repair.''')\ns=s.replace('expected eight-percent fitness','expected six-percent fitness')\ns=s.replace('''  An isolated local prototype completed stalled CoreMark with 4,198,165''','''  An initial isolated 16-bit prototype completed stalled CoreMark with 4,198,165''')\ns=s.replace('''  preliminary checks do not replace unchanged formal, directed prediction\n  recovery tests or median Gowin fitness evaluation. At this cycle count,\n  acceptance requires median Fmax above approximately 95.416 MHz.''','''  preliminary checks do not replace unchanged formal, directed prediction\n  recovery tests or median Gowin fitness evaluation. Its single placement-0\n  timing was 84.234 MHz, below the champion; its worst path remained\n  MEM-to-OC with an EX recovery path close behind. The final proposed\n  eight-bit EX predictor and upper-only MEM validator specifically reduce\n  that recovery logic and duplicated validation, but a win is unproven.\n  Record final prototype results below if available; do not reuse the\n  initial 16-bit cycle count as the final candidate's measured result.''')\ns=s.replace('  fitness_delta_pct: 8','  fitness_delta_pct: 6')\ns=s.replace('''      Add shared unsigned low-16 less-than and full-sign-aware signed''','''      Add shared unsigned low-byte less-than and full-sign-aware signed''')\ns=s.replace('''      existing EX/MEM branch_taken field, and defer conditional alignment''','''      existing EX/MEM branch_taken field to carr