{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_68", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r13s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261005-003-r13s2\ntitle: \"Predict relational branch conditions with 8-bit comparison and registered exact repair\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 217.29 at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed\n  CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent and predictor history was reviewed.\n  Smaller folded-PC tables, counter recoding and delayed control-flow\n  validation regressed. A return profile finds only 13,735 timed JALRs,\n  so return prediction alone has insufficient upside. Ordinary direction\n  policy improvements also save too few errors to justify larger tables.\n  The current full-width relational branch comparisons feed same-cycle\n  EX redirect, frontend flush and predictor training. A computational\n  branch-condition predictor can shorten that feedback while retaining\n  immediate EX correction of ordinary fetch-direction mistakes.\nhypothesis: |\n  Introduce one stateless computational predictor for relational branch\n  conditions. Keep BEQ and BNE exact with their existing full-width\n  equality checks. For BLTU/BGEU compare only rs1[7:0] and rs2[7:0],\n  complementing the less-than result for BGEU. For BLT/BGE use the true\n  32-bit sign bits: when rs1[31] differs from rs2[31], signed less-than\n  is rs1[31]; otherwise predict from unsigned low-8-bit less-than.\n  Complement this result for BGE. Read only registered OC/EX operands,\n  with no new forwarding or operand-range assumptions. Wider values\n  remain legal and are always checked against exact execution.\n\n  EX uses the provisional branch condition to correct the accepted fetch\n  direction immediately, using the existing direction-XOR recovery and\n  exact PC+immediate target. Qualify provisional taken with valid, legal\n  branch encoding and target alignment. Keep JAL/JALR resolution, link\n  values and alignment traps exact in EX. Preserve current EX advancement,\n  dmem/divider hold gating, older registered recovery priority and flush\n  behavior. Unlike r8s2, ordinary bimodal direction errors still recover\n  in EX; only a wrong computed relati\n…[7818 of 10890 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bf31dd19721b40e0]…\n-condition validation.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: |\n      Preserve exact RVFI and wrong-path-effect assertions. Add all four\n      relational branches with equal low halves and unequal high halves,\n      sign disagreement, negative operands, unsigned boundaries and both\n      mismatch directions. Cover speculative condition changes around\n      misaligned targets, exact BEQ/BNE, consecutive branches, retained\n      operands, wrong-path stores/divides, both bus stalls and older\n      multiply recovery. Check immediate ordinary direction correction,\n      once-only late repair and exact registered predictor training.\n  - file: test/test_mem_repair.py\n    description: |\n      Extend the existing registered repair tests to exact branch\n      validation, corrected successors and traps, branch-only mismatch,\n      no replay when effective successors agree, back-to-back training\n      events, MEM holds and recovery quarantine. Retain all multiply\n      validation and exact retirement coverage.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
