 every valid instruction,\nincluding PC+4 for ordinary instructions and suppressed misaligned control\ntransfers. Redirect and flush only when this successor differs from the\ncaptured prediction. Correctly predicted taken transfers accept the target\ninstruction without a bubble; predicted-taken/actually-not-taken and\nstale JALR targets recover to the resolved successor. Checking ordinary\ninstructions as well also repairs stale entries after instruction changes.\n\nTrain once when a valid instruction actually advances out of EX, never\nwhile EX/MEM is held by dmem backpressure. Allocate legal, aligned branches\nand jumps with their resolved control target, not the fall-through PC of a\nnot-taken branch. Initialize a cond\n…[23177 of 26249 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a737ceb19bf3bb6e]…\nd against exact execution.\n\nEX uses the provisional branch condition to correct the accepted fetch\ndirection immediately, using the existing direction-XOR recovery and\nexact PC+immediate target. Qualify provisional taken with valid, legal\nbranch encoding and target alignment. Keep JAL/JALR resolution, link\nvalues and alignment traps exact in EX. Preserve current EX advancement,\ndmem/divider hold gating, older registered recovery priority and flush\nbehavior. Unlike r8s2, ordinary bimodal direction errors still recover\nin EX; only a wrong computed relational condition needs late repair.\n\nCapture the raw provisional condition, before alignment qualification,\nin the existing EX/MEM branch_taken field, together with original\nfull-width architectural rs1/rs2 and the\nexisting exact branch_target. Existing bundles already carry these\nfields, so no extra operand bank or full-width prediction target is\nneeded. EX must not declare a conditional branch illegal based on its\napproximate condition: determine conditional ta\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
