{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2','title':'Capture load-history predictions in EX before MEM-to-OC forwarding','category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 217.29 at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Relevant history was reviewed: r9s2's 128-entry load-value predictor achieved good coverage and only 8,662 extra cycles, but its late lookup regressed Fmax; recent reports repeatedly identify MEM-to-OC as a limiting path. An isolated 16-entry variant added 166,929 cycles and reached only 76.779 MHz in placement option 0, with a 34-cell history-to-OC path. Smaller storage alone does not fix this. The promising predictor angle is early speculative lookup with a registered candidate, preserving large-table coverage while removing table selection and live memory data from OC forwarding.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one 128-entry direct-mapped advisory raw-word load history, indexed by aligned word-address bits [8:2], storing a 23-bit full upper-address tag, a 32-bit word and validity. Reset validity only; invalid tags and words must never become an available forwarding source. The architectural reference profile of the canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration ELF finds 514,383 address-history hits among 544,852 timed loads with accepted load/store updates. This sequential profile establishes potential coverage, not pipeline hit accuracy, cycle savings or correctness.\n\nPerform table selection in EX, one stage before a load needs MEM-to-OC forwarding. Derive only the seven-bit word index from the low nine bits of the registered architectural rs1 plus immediate; this is the exact low-address sum, not a guessed effective address. Read raw candidate word, stored tag and valid bit in parallel. Capture all three into new EX/MEM fields together with the actual full effective address. Do not compare tags or format the candidate before this register. Do not expose the combinational lookup to OC, change EX load availability or place a full-address addition followed by tag comparison on EX's return bypass. Lookup for nonloads can be unconditional; only a valid load may consume its captured candidate.\n\nIn MEM, compare the registered candidate tag with actual effective_addr[31:9] and combine it with captured validity. Format the registered predicted word using the load's real lane, width and signedness. Replace live dmemRData load forwarding with this registered candidate. A legal aligned hit becomes available only on the actual dmemReady acceptance, with existing final writer qualification. A miss leaves the nearest MEM load unavailable; dependent OC sources wait until exact WB data is available. Keep the EX unavailable-load interlock and the current one-bubble hit dependency timing. Never fall back to live dmemRData on the MEM-to-OC bypass.\n\nEvery load still issues its original memory request and commits the exact formatted bus result into MEM/WB. Validate accepted hit predictions against the actual raw bus word. Full-word equality is a sufficient certificate for every width and sign; differences in unused bytes may conservatively cause replay. Register a mismatch for a valid legal aligned load writing rd\"'!=x0 into the existing MEM/WB recovery bit, independently ORed with multiply mismatch. Preserve unconditional capture of the original pc_next repair target. Exact bus data and the equality comparator must have no combinational path to current OC availability, frontend recovery or memory enables.\n\nReuse existing registered older recovery: the original load retires exactly once with exact architectural value and original raw memory RVFI fields. Next-cycle recovery replays at its PC+4, quarantines younger MEM requests even when unready, squashes EX/OC/decode and saved operands, suppresses younger redirects and training, and cancels a younger divider or held result. Preserve multiply validation and its oldest-repair priority. Correct predictions add no pipeline stage or bubble; misses can add one consumer wait cycle.\n\nTrain the history at MEM from actual accepted, legal, aligned, nonquarantined memory operations. Loads fill exact raw bus words. Full-word stores allocate their exact word; matching partial stores merge enabled bytes, while a partial store with no matching tag cannot allocate unknown bytes. Gate updates by actual readiness, memory enables, !hold_wb and !older_recovery. Holding a transaction must never train repeatedly. Keep lookup outputs based on pre-write state at the EX capture edge. In particular, an older same-edge store may make an early candidate stale or leave a captured miss; validate stale hits and let misses wait for WB. Do not forward training writes into lookup or assume table coherence. Early lookup and its pipelined tag are prediction metadata, never permission to skip the real bus transaction.\n\nThe architectural mechanism differs from r9s2 by moving all array selection before the EX/MEM register; MEM-to-OC sees only registered prediction formatting and tag qualification. The seven-bit index is known from a short low-address sum without waiting for high address bits. Risks are low-index addition plus table read becoming an EX setup bottleneck, table storage/update fanout, stale candidates from immediate older stores, miss waits, and the remaining ALU-to-OC path. Actual vendor mapping and timing must establish the benefit; LUT-RAM inference is not assumed. Measure stalled CoreMark cycles because the earlier sequential profile does not model pre-write pipeline lookups.\n\nPreserve nret=1, every external port, all decoder/trap invariants, branch prediction policy, multiplier/divider arithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, operand retention and nearest-producer ordering, real bus handshakes, exact RVFI operands/results/memory/next-PC/order, and every evaluation gate. Run unchanged formal, meaningful predictor and pipeline tests, ready/stalled trace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/MMIO/bracket/completion/bounded-access validation, and median Gowin timing. Require (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046. The expected gain is an unproven estimate.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/load_predictor.sv','description':'''Add the 128-entry raw-word prediction history with low-word-index read, separate raw tag/valid outputs, valid-only reset, once-only accepted MEM updates, full-tag replacement and exact partial-store merging. Do not put lookup tag comparison or formatting inside this module's EX read path.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Extend EX/MEM with the captured candidate raw word, 23-bit tag and valid bit; preserve existing exact address, source, instruction, control and architectural next-PC fields. No extra IF, ID or OC metadata is needed.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Expose an exact seven-bit prediction index from the low-nine-bit registered rs1-plus-immediate sum. Capture supplied table word/tag/valid with the load at EX/MEM acceptance. Keep combinational prediction off EX bypass, preserve unavailable-load timing, all holds/squashes/divider payload behavior, and exact effective-address generation.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Qualify and format the captured prediction after the EX/MEM boundary for MEM-to-OC bypass; make misses wait for WB. Keep bus load formatting and retirement exact. Register accepted raw-word mismatches into existing older recovery without combinational validation fanout. Retain multiplication validation, memory alignment, transaction gating, WB retention and younger-memory quarantine.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Instantiate the advisory history, route EX lookup and candidate capture signals, and route accepted MEM raw load/store updates. Preserve external IO, recovery/hold priorities, sole retirement channel and order counter.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_load_predictor.py','description':'''Test valid-only reset and invalid masking, full-tag aliases, accepted loads and full/partial stores, every byte lane, held updates and pre-write read/write semantics. Exercise deliberately stale data rather than assuming history coherence.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_mem_repair.py','description':'''Extend exact retirement and registered quarantine tests to load hits/misses, arbitrary stale candidates, same-edge older stores, alignment faults and recovery arbitration. Preserve all existing multiplier recovery assertions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain architectural checks and verify early candidate capture, hit/miss dependency timing, high-address aliases, byte/halfword formatting, changed memory data, retained sources, both bus stalls, x0, younger stores/branches/JALR/dividers, recovery cancellation, and exact RVFI. Adapt only internal and prediction-specific timing observations.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2','title':'Capture load-history predictions in EX before MEM-to-OC forwarding','category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 217.29 at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Relevant history was reviewed: r9s2's 128-entry load-value predictor achieved good coverage and only 8,662 extra cycles, but its late lookup regressed Fmax; recent reports repeatedly identify MEM-to-OC as a limiting path. An isolated 16-entry variant added 166,929 cycles and reached only 76.779 MHz in placement option 0, with a 34-cell history-to-OC path. Smaller storage alone does not fix this. The promising predictor angle is early speculative lookup with a registered candidate, preserving large-table coverage while removing table selection and live memory data from OC forwarding.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one 128-entry direct-mapped advisory raw-word load history, indexed by aligned word-address bits [8:2], storing a 23-bit full upper-address tag, a 32-bit word and validity. Reset validity only; invalid tags and words must never become an available forwarding source. The architectural reference profile of the canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration ELF finds 514,383 address-history hits among 544,852 timed loads with accepted load/store updates. This sequential profile establishes potential coverage, not pipeline hit accuracy, cycle savings or correctness.\n\nPerform table selection in EX, one stage before a load needs MEM-to-OC forwarding. Derive only the seven-bit word index from the low nine bits of the registered architectural rs1 plus immediate; this is the exact low-address sum, not a guessed effective address. Read raw candidate word, stored tag and valid bit in parallel. Capture all three into new EX/MEM fields together with the actual full effective address. Do not compare tags or format the candidate before this register. Do not expose the combinational lookup to OC, change EX load availability or place a full-address addition followed by tag comparison on EX's return bypass. Lookup for nonloads can be unconditional; only a valid load may consume its captured candidate.\n\nIn MEM, compare the registered candidate tag with actual effective_addr[31:9] and combine it with captured validity. Format the registered predicted word using the load's real lane, width and signedness. Replace live dmemRData load forwarding with this registered candidate. A legal aligned hit becomes available only on the actual dmemReady acceptance, with existing final writer qualification. A miss leaves the nearest MEM load unavailable; dependent OC sources wait until exact WB data is available. Keep the EX unavailable-load interlock and the current one-bubble hit dependency timing. Never fall back to live dmemRData on the MEM-to-OC bypass.\n\nEvery load still issues its original memory request and commits the exact formatted bus result into MEM/WB. Validate accepted hit predictions against the actual raw bus word. Full-word equality is a sufficient certificate for every width and sign; differences in unused bytes may conservatively cause replay. Register a mismatch for a valid legal aligned load writing rd\"'!=x0 into the existing MEM/WB recovery bit, independently ORed with multiply mismatch. Preserve unconditional capture of the original pc_next repair target. Exact bus data and the equality comparator must have no combinational path to current OC availability, frontend recovery or memory enables.\n\nReuse existing registered older recovery: the original load retires exactly once with exact architectural value and original raw memory RVFI fields. Next-cycle recovery replays at its PC+4, quarantines younger MEM requests even when unready, squashes EX/OC/decode and saved operands, suppresses younger redirects and training, and cancels a younger divider or held result. Preserve multiply validation and its oldest-repair priority. Correct predictions add no pipeline stage or bubble; misses can add one consumer wait cycle.\n\nTrain the history at MEM from actual accepted, legal, aligned, nonquarantined memory operations. Loads fill exact raw bus words. Full-word stores allocate their exact word; matching partial stores merge enabled bytes, while a partial store with no matching tag cannot allocate unknown bytes. Gate updates by actual readiness, memory enables, !hold_wb and !older_recovery. Holding a transaction must never train repeatedly. Keep lookup outputs based on pre-write state at the EX capture edge. In particular, an older same-edge store may make an early candidate stale or leave a captured miss; validate stale hits and let misses wait for WB. Do not forward training writes into lookup or assume table coherence. Early lookup and its pipelined tag are prediction metadata, never permission to skip the real bus transaction.\n\nThe architectural mechanism differs from r9s2 by moving all array selection before the EX/MEM register; MEM-to-OC sees only registered prediction formatting and tag qualification. The seven-bit index is known from a short low-address sum without waiting for high address bits. Risks are low-index addition plus table read becoming an EX setup bottleneck, table storage/update fanout, stale candidates from immediate older stores, miss waits, and the remaining ALU-to-OC path. Actual vendor mapping and timing must establish the benefit; LUT-RAM inference is not assumed. Measure stalled CoreMark cycles because the earlier sequential profile does not model pre-write pipeline lookups.\n\nPreserve nret=1, every external port, all decoder/trap invariants, branch prediction policy, multiplier/divider arithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, operand retention and nearest-producer ordering, real bus handshakes, exact RVFI operands/results/memory/next-PC/order, and every evaluation gate. Run unchanged formal, meaningful predictor and pipeline tests, ready/stalled trace cosim, canonical CoreMark CRC/MMIO/bracket/completion/bounded-access validation, and median Gowin timing. Require (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046. The expected gain is an unproven estimate.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/load_predictor.sv','description':'''Add the 128-entry raw-word prediction history with low-word-index read, separate raw tag/valid outputs, valid-only reset, once-only accepted MEM updates, full-tag replacement and exact partial-store merging. Do not put lookup tag comparison or formatting inside this module's EX read path.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'''Extend EX/MEM with the captured candidate raw word, 23-bit tag and valid bit; preserve existing exact address, source, instruction, control and architectural next-PC fields. No extra IF, ID or OC metadata is needed.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Expose an exact seven-bit prediction index from the low-nine-bit registered rs1-plus-immediate sum. Capture supplied table word/tag/valid with the load at EX/MEM acceptance. Keep combinational prediction off EX bypass, preserve unavailable-load timing, all holds/squashes/divider payload behavior, and exact effective-address generation.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Qualify and format the captured prediction after the EX/MEM boundary for MEM-to-OC bypass; make misses wait for WB. Keep bus load formatting and retirement exact. Register accepted raw-word mismatches into existing older recovery without combinational validation fanout. Retain multiplication validation, memory alignment, transaction gating, WB retention and younger-memory quarantine.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Instantiate the advisory history, route EX lookup and candidate capture signals, and route accepted MEM raw load/store updates. Preserve external IO, recovery/hold priorities, sole retirement channel and order counter.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_load_predictor.py','description':'''Test valid-only reset and invalid masking, full-tag aliases, accepted loads and full/partial stores, every byte lane, held updates and pre-write read/write semantics. Exercise deliberately stale data rather than assuming history coherence.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_mem_repair.py','description':'''Extend exact retirement and registered quarantine tests to load hits/misses, arbitrary stale candidates, same-edge older stores, alignment faults and recovery arbitration. Preserve all existing multiplier recovery assertions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain architectural checks and verify early candidate capture, hit/miss dependency timing, high-address aliases, byte/halfword formatting, changed memory data, retained sources, both bus stalls, x0, younger stores/branches/JALR/dividers, recovery cancellation, and exact RVFI. Adapt only internal and prediction-specific timing observations.\n'''}]}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,default_flow_style=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nprint('Updated and schema-validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "Updated and schema-validated: cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
