{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"agent_message","text":"The synchronous layout reduced the count to 1,458 registers, but tag comparison still produced the worst path. The final refinement removes address tags and validates every prediction that OC captures. Aliases remain safe because loads retire with exact bus data and a wrong consumed prediction triggers replay."}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_57", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r14s2.yaml')\nd={'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r14s2','title':'Untagged synchronous load-value prediction with use-qualified replay','category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 217.29 at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 measured CoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent. Relevant predictor attempts were reviewed, especially r9s2's tagged load-history predictor, which regressed timing despite good coverage. Isolated local probes found that a small late table still adds a long OC path; a large early table needs synchronous byte-bank reads to avoid thousands of registers. With that mapping fixed, the tagged prototype reached 81.471 MHz in placement option 0 and its worst path was the tag memory through MEM qualification to OC, with 29 cells. The most promising remaining load-predictor angle is to remove tags entirely and register the predicted word before MEM, validating only predictions actually captured by OC.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one advisory 128-entry raw-word load-value predictor indexed by word-address bits [8:2]. Each entry stores only 32 data bits and validity: no address tags, address-hit comparison, cached permissions or coherence assumptions. Index aliases are permitted prediction errors and are always checked before affected younger instructions can retire.\n\nRead the predictor synchronously on the EX/MEM acceptance edge. EX derives the exact seven-bit word index using the low nine bits of its registered architectural rs1 plus immediate. Organize data as four independently writable 128-by-8 byte banks with simple synchronous read outputs and no data reset. Use a separate validity plane; reset table validity and the captured candidate-valid flag. The predictor's registered raw-word output and candidate validity form a sidecar to EX/MEM, rather than embedding resettable candidate-data flops in the wide EX/MEM struct. Capture both on the same enabled edge as the actual load address; hold both during dmem stalls. Gate read capture by advancing EX, excluding older recovery and divider wait; div completion and bubbles may read irrelevant candidates safely. Do not add a pipeline stage or move load availability into EX. Ensure the vendor infers memory and its output registers; the prior asynchronous-capture probe produced excessive flops.\n\nIn MEM, format that registered raw candidate with the load's actual lane, width and signedness. A valid candidate is available only for a valid legal aligned nonzero-destination load on its real dmemReady handshake and current writer eligibility. Do not perform an address-tag check. Keep EX loads unavailable, preserving the current one-bubble load-use timing on warm candidates. Cold invalid slots leave the nearest MEM producer unavailable until exact WB; never fall back to live dmemRData on the MEM-to-OC path. Arbitrary candidate contents may exist while invalid, but cannot be captured as a ready architectural source.\n\nExpose a one-cycle OC indication that a MEM source is actually captured. It is true when a valid nonflushed OC instruction captures an unsaved, ready source selected from MEM, whether into OC/EX on advance or into a saved source while held. Check both raw register source fields, preserving the current operand and RVFI conventions. Already saved sources do not count again; unavailable MEM sources never count; reset and older recovery suppress capture. This indication observes existing selections and capture conditions and must not change forwarding, hazard readiness or source selection.\n\nEvery load still performs its original bus transaction and commits the exact formatted bus result and raw RVFI memory data. Compare the captured candidate raw word against actual dmemRData only for an accepted valid legal aligned load with a nonzero destination. Register replay when candidate-valid, OC captured a MEM source, and the words differ. Full-word equality suffices for all load widths and signs; differences in unused bytes may conservatively replay. An unused wrong candidate needs no repair because no younger operand contains it. Retire the original load exactly once with the exact value in either case. Keep equality and the use indication off current bypass readiness, frontend control and memory enables; they feed the recovery register only.\n\nOR this load mismatch with the existing independently qualified multiply mismatch at MEM/WB. Reuse the current original pc_next recovery target and next-cycle older repair priority. Quarantine younger MEM requests even if unready, squash younger EX/OC/decode and saved operands, suppress younger redirect/training, and cancel younger divider state or held completion. This also handles a predicted source saved while an unrelated younger division holds EX. All younger work that could contain a consumed wrong prediction is discarded before retirement or a memory side effect.\n\nLearn once from accepted legal aligned nonquarantined MEM transactions, independent of whether the current candidate was used or right. Loads and full-word stores fill all four banks and validate their indexed slot. Partial stores update their enabled byte banks only when that indexed slot is already valid; do not allocate unknown remaining bytes on an invalid slot. With no tags, a partial store may merge bytes belonging to another address: that result remains an arbitrary advisory candidate and is safe only through exact validation. Never treat the history as a memory cache or suppress a bus read. Qualify writes with real readiness, enabled memory operation, \"'!hold_wb, !older_recovery and !reset. Keep synchronous pre-write read semantics on same-index load/store edges; stale early candidates are expected and recover when used.\n\nThe intended benefit is a short registered candidate-to-OC data path and a one-bit validity qualification, eliminating live BRAM return timing and full-tag qualification. Compared with r9s2, lookup is one edge earlier, data banks infer synchronous FPGA memory, tags are absent and recovery is use-qualified. No tag miss waiting remains after warmup. Costs are extra memory blocks, byte-formatting logic, raw-word mismatch replays, cold waits and the remaining EX-result return path. Aliasing accuracy and store-read timing must be measured in RTL; sequential history coverage does not establish this candidate'\"'s accuracy or fitness. Do not assume loaded values, address ranges, memory stability or predictor correctness in formal builds.\n\nPreserve nret=1 and all external ports, existing branch prediction, exact real and ALTOPS arithmetic, decoder defaults and reserved-encoding traps, bus handshakes, alignment behavior, nearest producer priority, source retention, original RVFI operands/results/memory/PC/order, and every hard invariant. Run unchanged formal, directed candidate/capture/recovery tests, ready and stalled trace cosims, canonical 2K CoreMark CRC/MMIO/bracket/completion/bounded-access checks, and median vendor Gowin timing. Require (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046. Expected gain is an estimate with low confidence, not a measured win.\n''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n{'file':'rtl/load_predictor.sv','description':'''Add the untagged 128-entry predictor with four independently written byte banks, synchronous read outputs, valid-only reset and once-only accepted memory training. Preserve pre-write same-index semantics, cold invalid masking, full-word allocation and advisory partial-store updates without unknown-byte allocation.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'''Expose the exact low-address word index and a read-capture enable matching EX/MEM advancement and holds. Keep lookup off EX bypass, retain unavailable EX loads and exact address/branch/arithmetic generation. Predictor data output registers are an EX/MEM sidecar, with no extra stage or resettable data fields in the pipeline struct.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/operand_stage.sv','description':'''Observe actual unsaved ready MEM-source capture into OC/EX or retained source storage and expose a once-per-capture use indication. Include both existing source fields, suppress reset/flush and already-saved selections, and preserve all original mux, hold, availability and nearest-producer behavior.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Forward formatted registered predictions on valid warm accepted loads and wait for exact WB on cold slots. Keep bus reads and exact retirement intact; register raw-word mismatch only when OC captured the prediction, ORed with existing multiply recovery. Preserve alignment traps, WB retention, original RVFI memory fields and younger-memory quarantine.\n'''},\n{'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'''Wire the synchronous history sidecar, EX index/read enable, accepted MEM raw load/store updates and OC capture-use indication. Preserve every external port, all recovery and stall priorities, divider cancellation, sole retirement channel and order counter.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_load_predictor.py','description':'''Check cold validity, synchronous lookup latency, held read outputs, all byte banks and lanes, full and partial writes, disabled training, pre-write read/write collisions and deliberately aliased or stale candidates. Avoid assuming untagged entries are coherent memory copies.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_mem_repair.py','description':'''Test exact load retirement, no replay for an unused wrong candidate, replay for every consumed wrong candidate, raw-versus-formatted equality, x0 and faults, cold slots, memory backpressure and arbitration with original multiplication recovery. Retain all existing architectural assertions.\n'''},\n{'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Cover immediate and spaced load consumers, both raw source fields, matching saved sources during EX holds, alias and stale-data failures, same-edge older stores, all widths/signs, both bus stalls, younger memory/control/divider work, cancellation and exact RVFI. Check prediction validity remains synchronized with held EX/MEM and no consumed error escapes older repair.\n'''}]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):pass\ndef rep(d,s):return d.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',s,style='|' if '\\\\n' in s else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,rep)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=88))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.load(open('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json')))\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Final mechanism written and schema-valid:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
