/REMU expressions with one shared unsigned\\nmagnitude divider that produces quotient and remainder together. Implement\\nan explicitly unrolled radix-2 restoring recurrence with compile-time\\nwidths: step k consumes the next dividend bit, has a k-bit candidate\\nremainder, and subtracts only divisor[k-1:0] using a k+1-bit difference.\\nAccept that subtraction only when its borrow is clear and every omitted\\nupper divisor bit is zero. Thus the subtractors grow from 1 to 32 bits,\\nrather than carrying full-width arithmetic through every step. Use the\\nsubtraction's borrow to select the new remainder and emit the quotient\\nbit, avoid\n…[496260 of 499332 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bd2665f904d714ff]…\nrces during EX holds, alias and stale-data failures, same-edge older stores, all widths/signs, both bus stalls, younger memory/control/divider work, cancellation and exact RVFI. Check prediction validity remains synchronized with held EX/MEM and no consumed error escapes older repair.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 192.62, \"delta_pct\": -11.35, \"vs_baseline\": 1489.27, \"fmax_mhz\": 81.586, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4235685, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4622, \"ff\": 1458, \"seeds\": [77.085, 81.586, 81.586], \"perturbations\": [[0, 77.085, 12], [1, 81.586, 12], [2, 81.586, 12]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 10, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_oc/reg_q.rs1_val_3_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_23_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -7.973, \"arrival_ns\": 18.267, \"logic_cells\": 36, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T09:40:59.563347Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
