{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines() if s.strip()]\nfor r in rows:\n if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261005-003-r8s2','hyp-20261005-003-r11s2','hyp-20261005-003-r12s2','hyp-20261005-001-r8s0','hyp-20261005-001-r9s0']:\n  print(r['id'],r['title'])\n  print(r.get('critical_path',{}))\n  print(r['hypothesis']['motivation'])\n  if r['id'] in ['hyp-20261005-003-r8s2','hyp-20261005-003-r11s2']: print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261005-001-r8s0 Remove redundant outcome qualification from predictor training data\n{'from': 'cpu/u_fwd/fwd_rs1_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.pc_next_21_s0', 'slack_ns': -11.235, 'arrival_ns': 21.529, 'logic_cells': 42, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nThe champion scores 188.51 at 79.208 MHz with 4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its 18.733 ns worst path starts at MEM/WB load data and traverses WB forwarding and EX branch resolution into the IF direction table. The training data is actual_taken, which repeats validity, branch-kind, legality and misalignment qualification already enforced by branch_train_en. This puts extra logic and shared recovery fanout after the late comparator. LESSONS.md is absent; the prior micro_opt attempts and recent outcomes were reviewed. Larger local rewrites exposed other critical paths without exceeding the acceptance threshold; a minimal exact data-path factorization is preferable here.\nhyp-20261005-003-r8s2 Speculate next PC through EX and register exact control-flow validation\n{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.mem_to_reg_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.789, 'arrival_ns': 17.083, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_wb', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nThe champion scores 188.51 at median Gowin Fmax 79.208 MHz with 4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst path runs from MEM/WB load data through forwarded EX branch comparison into the IF direction table (18.733 ns). Merely registering training exposed the remaining comparison-to-recovery fanout and measured only 77.719 MHz with unchanged cycles, so that limited version is not the final proposal. LESSONS.md is absent; prior predictor attempts and outcomes were inspected. Bimodal/JAL prediction previously improved fitness, while arithmetic carry/shift prediction, narrow multiply certification and nine-bit multiply prediction failed acceptance. The opportunity is to let the existing branch prediction carry execution past EX and valid\n…[11057 of 14129 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b56e959612469123]…\ncceptance requires median Fmax above 95.380556 MHz;\nin general require (Fmax_new/91.186)*(4196601/cycles_new) > 1.046.\n\nhyp-20261005-003-r12s2 Reduce branch-table aliases with a compact folded-PC bimodal predictor\n{'from': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_oc/reg_q.alu_b_val_29_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.341, 'arrival_ns': 17.635, 'logic_cells': 9, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_mem', 'cpu/u_oc']}\nThe champion scores 217.29 at 91.186 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. LESSONS.md is absent; the predictor history and recent\noutcomes were reviewed. Delayed control-flow validation, arithmetic\nreplay and confidence-plane counter recoding have regressed. The\nexisting 64-entry direction table indexes only PC[7:2], so unrelated\nbranches separated by 256 bytes repeatedly overwrite the same counters.\nA smaller table with a folded PC index can reduce that interference\nwhile reducing lookup and training mux size. This targets the predictor\npolicy and capacity without adding a pipeline stage or recovery latency.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
