{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(line)\n print(e['id'],e['category'],e.get('fitness'),e.get('cycles'),e.get('fmax_mhz'))\n if e['category']=='predictor':\n  h=e.get('hypothesis',{})\n  print(h.get('hypothesis','') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)\n  print('notes:',e.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-df5bec5 micro_opt 12.12 4491485 5.442\nhyp-20261005-001-r1s0 micro_opt 13.11 4491485 5.888\nhyp-20261005-002-r1s1 structural 104.51 4491817 46.944\nhyp-20261005-003-r1s2 predictor 13.23 4208674 5.568\nAdd one 32-entry direct-mapped, fully tagged next-PC predictor indexed by\nfetch PC[6:2]. Each entry contains a valid bit, PC[31:7] tag, an aligned\ntarget address, and a two-bit saturating taken counter. An invalid entry,\ntag miss, or counter below 2 predicts PC+4; a hit with counter at least 2\npredicts the stored target. Use PC-only combinational lookup in parallel\nwith instruction fetch, without an additional fetch stage or an imem-data\ndependency. Reset valid bits; other entry fields need no reset and must\nnever influence a prediction while invalid.\n\nCarry the exact predicted successor used to advance the fetch PC through\nIF/ID and ID/EX. At EX, keep the existing forwarded branch comparisons,\nJAL/JALR target calculation, link value, and alignment/trap behavior.\nCompute the actual architectural successor for every valid instruction,\nincluding PC+4 for ordinary instructions and suppressed misaligned control\ntransfers. Redirect and flush only when this successor differs from the\ncaptured prediction. Correctly predicted taken transfers accept the target\ninstruction without a bubble; predicted-taken/actually-not-taken and\nstale JALR targets recover to the resolved successor. Checking ordinary\ninstructions as well also repairs stale entries after instruction changes.\n\nTrain once when a valid instruction actually advances out of EX, never\nwhile EX/MEM is held by dmem backpressure. Allocate legal, aligned branches\nand jumps with their resolved control target, not the fall-through PC of a\nnot-taken branch. Initialize a conditional branch counter to 2 for taken\nor 1 for not taken, then saturate on later outcomes; initialize jumps to 3\nand refresh their targets. Replace conflicting tags rather than training\ntheir old counters. Invalidate a matching stale entry when a non-control\ninstruction resolves, and clear pre\n…[5423 of 8495 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5f1781d536605a8e]…\npeline\nstage, altered retirement width, memory interface, or arithmetic change.\n\nExpect roughly 8 percent higher fitness from fewer taken-control bubbles\nwith a small direction table and a one-bit conditional recovery cone.\nThe architectural profile suggests about 291,938 fewer redirect bubbles\nbefore pipeline-training latency and overlap with bus stalls, equivalent\nto 6.5 percent of the champion's counted cycles. The estimate assumes the\nsimpler repair/hazard path preserves or modestly improves Fmax.\nThis is an unmeasured estimate; JALR remains a penalty and direction-table\naliases or the imem-to-target-adder path can limit the gain. Validate with\nthe unchanged formal and CoreMark cosimulation/CRC gates and median Gowin\ntiming. At unchanged Fmax, acceptance needs counted cycles below about\n4,294,280; in general require (Fmax_new / 46.944 MHz) times\n(4,491,817 / cycles_new) greater than 1.046. Preserve nret=1, every external\nport, exact retirement ordering, decoder legality, and all hard invariants.\n\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The current bimodal predictor already removes most taken-branch bubbles, so improving direction accuracy alone has limited room to help. I’m investigating whether it can also hide load-to-branch waits by letting a dependent branch advance on its prediction and verifying the loaded operand one stage later."}}
