{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predictor|return.address|gshare|bimodal|jalr|prediction|ras' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share and width-prune the combinational DIV/REM datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the four real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with one shared unsigned\\nmagnitude divider that produces quotient and remainder together. Implement\\nan explicitly unrolled radix-2 restoring recurrence with compile-time\\nwidths: step k consumes the next dividend bit, has a k-bit candidate\\nremainder, and subtracts only divisor[k-1:0] using a k+1-bit difference.\\nAccept that subtraction only when its borrow is clear and every omitted\\nupper divisor bit is zero. Thus the subtractors grow from 1 to 32 bits,\\nrather than carrying full-width arithmetic through every step. Use the\\nsubtraction's borrow to select the new remainder and emit the quotient\\nbit, avoiding a separat\n…[98965 of 102037 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:56b2c32d98d7bc20]…\ntions,\\nrd=x0, high-product variants, forwarded and loaded operands, and bus\\nstalls at advancement/recovery. Check exact RVFI operands/results,\\nunique retirement, no wrong-path memory effects or divider launch,\\nolder-repair priority, correct replay PC and bubble-free matches.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 138.64, \"delta_pct\": 17.74, \"vs_baseline\": 1043.89, \"fmax_mhz\": 58.252, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4201709, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3371, \"ff\": 949, \"seeds\": [55.109, 58.252, 58.252], \"perturbations\": [[0, 55.109, 15], [1, 58.252, 15], [2, 58.252, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -13.146, \"arrival_ns\": 23.44, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T01:24:36.438029Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 3}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
