{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|predict|branch|return|BTB|gshare|RAS' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261005-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Share and width-prune the combinational DIV/REM datapath\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The only recorded experiment is the baseline: 12.12 fitness at 5.442 MHz,\\nwith a 199.837 ns, 156-cell worst path through forwarding and the execute\\nALU. The ALU expresses signed and unsigned division and remainder as four\\nseparate arithmetic expressions. These deep combinational arithmetic\\ncones are a strong candidate for the unusually low Fmax, and replicating\\nthem also creates placement and routing pressure in the 12,312-LUT design.\\nA combinational divider optimization can improve clock frequency without\\nchanging CoreMark's cycle count or the pipeline's stall behavior.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the four real DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU expressions with one shared unsigned\\nmagnitude divider that produces quotient and remainder together. Implement\\nan explicitly unrolled radix-2 restoring recurrence with compile-time\\nwidths: step k consumes the next dividend bit, has a k-bit candidate\\nremainder, and subtracts only divisor[k-1:0] using a k+1-bit difference.\\nAccept that subtraction only when its borrow is clear and every omitted\\nupper divisor bit is zero. Thus the subtractors grow from 1 to 32 bits,\\nrather than carrying full-width arithmetic through every step. Use the\\nsubtraction's borrow to select the new remainder and emit the quotient\\nbit, avoiding a separat\n…[243803 of 246875 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0c4e7c28855c6fb2]…\nxact RVFI\\ndata, order, memory quarantine, redirect and divider-cancellation\\nassertions. Exercise additional narrow-range misses followed by\\ndependent arithmetic, memory, control and division instructions,\\nincluding both forwarding paths, repeated misses and bus holds.\\n\"}], \"outcome\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 160.27, \"delta_pct\": -10.23, \"vs_baseline\": 1222.36, \"fmax_mhz\": 68.394, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4267360, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3752, \"ff\": 1003, \"seeds\": [66.746, 68.394, 68.394], \"perturbations\": [[0, 66.746, 16], [1, 68.394, 14], [2, 68.394, 14]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 4, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_fwd/fwd_rs2_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/direction_q_direction_q_RAMREG_1_G[6]_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -9.982, \"arrival_ns\": 20.276, \"logic_cells\": 41, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 16, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-05T04:37:06.253847Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
