{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python -u - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval import gowin\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/b62664fd/0cebedcc/control_isolated_probe')\nrs=gowin.build_all(Path.cwd(),root/'rtl','fpga/core_bench_si.sv',root/'timing')\n(root/'timing_result.json').write_text(json.dumps(rs,indent=2))\nprint(json.dumps(gowin.summarize(rs),indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"placement_failed\": false,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 81.561,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    81.692,\n    81.561,\n    81.561\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      81.692,\n      12\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      81.561,\n      8\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      81.561,\n      8\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"lut4\": 4294,\n  \"ff\": 1342,\n  \"lutram\": 55,\n  \"bsram\": 4,\n  \"dsp\": 6,\n  \"logic_levels\": 12,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.mem_to_reg_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_26_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.241,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 17.535,\n    \"logic_cells\": 12,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_wb\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r8s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r8s2',\n 'title':'Speculate next PC through EX and register exact control-flow validation',\n 'category':'predictor',\n 'motivation':'''The champion scores 188.51 at median Gowin Fmax 79.208 MHz with 4,201,709 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst path runs from MEM/WB load data through forwarded EX branch comparison into the IF direction table (18.733 ns). Merely registering training exposed the remaining comparison-to-recovery fanout and measured only 77.719 MHz with unchanged cycles, so that limited version is not the final proposal. LESSONS.md is absent; prior predictor attempts and outcomes were inspected. Bimodal/JAL prediction previously improved fitness, while arithmetic carry/shift prediction, narrow multiply certification and nine-bit multiply prediction failed acceptance. The opportunity is to let the existing branch prediction carry execution past EX and validate control flow behind registered operands, removing forwarded comparisons from same-cycle frontend recovery.''',\n'hypothesis':'''Extend the current instruction-qualified next-PC prediction into one scheme with registered MEM validation. Retain the existing 64-entry two-bit conditional direction table, weakly-taken reset and exact immediate JAL prediction. Add a small eight-entry, direct-mapped, fully tagged last-target bank for legal JALR, indexed by fetch PC[4:2], storing PC[31:5], target[31:2] and valid. A qualified aligned-target hit supplies the predicted JALR next PC; a miss predicts PC+4. Reset valid bits; unknown invalid tag/target storage must never affect lookup. The validated decoder remains the authority for instruction legality. Do not add a return stack, history predictor, fetch queue or arithmetic speculation.\n\nCarry the exact predicted successor accepted by fetch through IF/ID and ID/EX alongside the existing conditional predicted-taken bit. EX computes architectural source forwarding, direct targets, the JALR rs1+immediate target with bit zero cleared and PC+4 link values, but no branch/JALR redirect or predictor training depends on forwarded operand comparisons in EX. Capture original full-width source operands, the resolved target, predicted direction and predicted successor in EX/MEM. Reuse its pc_next as the predicted successor for JALR if convenient. For branches, target calculation is PC+immediate and prediction direction alone selects the provisional successor. Do not leave an unused generic EX redirect-target mux whose data still depends on branch_cond: tie absent EX redirects off and explicitly remove their timed comparison cone. JAL alignment is known from the immediate; preserve its current trap and link suppression.\n\nIn MEM resolve conditional branches exactly from the registered original operands. Effective taken means a legal condition-true branch with aligned target. Validate direction with effective-taken XOR captured predicted-taken. Validate JALR independently by comparing its captured prediction directly with the registered resolved JALR target; OR in its alignment fault. Do not compare JALR prediction with a generic resolved-next-PC mux: that mux also depends on branch comparison and would put two full-width validation cones in series. Use separate conditional and indirect checks, combining only their qualified one-bit mismatch outputs. Correctly predicted control transfers incur no bubble. All architectural RVFI next PCs are selected from exact resolution in MEM, never from speculation.\n\nRegister a control-flow repair bit and exact target at the existing MEM/WB boundary, combining it with the current registered multiplication repair as one oldest-instruction recovery record. Clock the target independently of the mismatch enable. The resolving older instruction retires exactly once. On the next cycle the registered repair drives the current immediate-priority frontend redirect and ID/EX squash, quarantines every younger MEM memory request and clears younger EX/MEM work, even when that younger bus is unready. Preserve divider cancellation, suppress younger divider start/wait and predictor events, and retain the current dmem hold and WB forwarding semantics. Correct predictions keep ordinary forwarding and advancement. A misprediction has a longer recovery penalty than the present EX resolution; measure its cost rather than assuming cycle count is preserved.\n\nHandle a taken misaligned conditional target in MEM with the existing trap/PC+4 behavior and exclude misaligned targets from direction training even when not taken. Handle misaligned JALR in MEM with trap, PC+4 and suppressed link write. Force a registered replay for every otherwise legal misaligned JALR, even if predicted successor equals PC+4: EX may already have forwarded its speculative link, and younger consumers must be replayed with the original architectural register value. Keep full-width operands and the present decoder default-illegal and reserved-encoding behavior. No prediction assumption becomes an architectural operand restriction or trap criterion.\n\nCapture predictor training events only for a legal aligned control instruction actually accepted by MEM, excluding hold_wb and existing older repair. Their registered PC/index, exact direction or target feed IF on the following edge. Read the then-current direction counter when consuming an event, so back-to-back same-index events accumulate without stale counter snapshots. Ordinary branch or JALR repair must still train its own resolving instruction; its registered event coincides with that repair and must not be canceled by it. Quarantined younger MEM instructions emit no event. Invalid cycles clear event valid. Pending valid events drain once even if the following instruction is held or dividing. Preserve accepting-edge pre-write lookup semantics and capture PC/prediction metadata only with actual fetch acceptance.\n\nRetain nret=1 and all external ports, actual RVFI source data, exact arithmetic and ALTOPS formulas, decoder legality, memory alignment/side-effect checks, retirement ordering and every evaluation invariant. This is one next-PC speculation/verification change; existing arithmetic prediction remains unchanged. Verify misprediction recovery for both branch directions, target-bank miss/hit/alias/stale target, JALR dependency forwarding, target misalignment, wrong-path stores/divides, repeated control transfers, independent bus stalls and older multiply repair. Run unchanged formal, all ready/stalled trace cosims, canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/bracket validation and median vendor Gowin timing. Acceptance requires (Fmax_new/79.208)*(4,201,709/cycles_new)>1.046. Principal risks are extra misprediction cycles, target-bank routing, RAM inference and a new MEM validation limit. Preliminary measurements will be recorded below; they are not substitutes for implementation-phase correctness gates.''',\n 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'medium'},\n 'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/if_stage.sv','description':'Retain instruction-qualified bimodal/direct-JAL prediction. Add the eight-entry valid/tagged aligned JALR target bank, qualification and PC+4 miss policy; emit the exact predicted successor. Consume registered MEM direction/target events using current counter state. Reset valid/direction state and preserve accept, repair priority and pre-edge lookup semantics.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core_pkg.sv','description':'Carry predicted successor in IF/ID and ID/EX; add accepted conditional prediction metadata to EX/MEM. Keep original full-width operands and targets. Use existing EX/MEM pc_next as the captured JALR predicted successor or add an explicit field. Keep RVFI payloads architectural at MEM/WB.'},\n {'file':'rtl/id_stage.sv','description':'Capture exact predicted successor with its instruction, PC and direction only when ID/EX advances; hold and clear all prediction metadata with the existing bundle. Preserve decode legality and prepared operands.'},\n {'file':'rtl/ex_stage.sv','description':'Remove timed conditional/JALR recovery and training from EX. Capture registered original operands, resolved direct/JALR targets, direction and predicted successor for MEM verification; keep link generation and ordinary execution. Explicitly eliminate EX branch-condition-dependent redirect-target selection. Retain direct-JAL misalignment behavior; move conditional/JALR alignment verification to MEM without changing architectural traps.'},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'Resolve conditional direction from registered full-width operands; validate direction with one bit and JALR prediction directly against its registered target using an independent equality cone. Produce exact architectural next PC and trap/link suppression. Extend registered older recovery with these mismatches and compulsory replay for misaligned JALR. Reuse existing quarantine/divider-cancellation protocol, register predictor events once on accepted non-quarantined MEM work and always commit exact existing multiplication results.'},\n {'file':'rtl/core.sv','description':'Wire registered MEM training into IF and unify control-flow/multiplication repair with the current older-priority squash and quarantine wiring. Keep top-level ports, nret, immediate registered-repair priority, fetch acceptance, dmem hold qualification and retirement boundary unchanged. Rename internal mul_repair to older_repair if useful and update all consumers consistently.'},\n {'file':'test/test_fetch_predictor.py','description':'Preserve direct prediction, instruction qualification, deterministic reset and pre-write semantics; add target-bank reset, misses, hits, full tag aliases, replacement and target changes. Check exact accepted successor and one-time ordered registered training. Adapt packed-bundle decoding to added prediction metadata while preserving architectural assertions.'},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'Update timing-specific predictor/recovery scoreboards for MEM resolution and registered repair while retaining every architectural, RVFI, exact arithmetic, memory, trap, forwarding and divider assertion. Require correct-prediction bubble-free behavior, both direction repairs, stale JALR target recovery, compulsory misaligned-JALR replay, event ordering, no wrong-path memory effects and older multiply priority under independent imem/dmem stalls.'}\n ]}\nclass Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper): pass\ndef represent_str(dumper,value):\n return dumper.represent_scalar('tag:yaml.org,2002:str',value,style='|' if '\\\\n' in value or len(value)>100 else None)\nDumper.add_representer(str,represent_str)\np.write_text(yaml.dump(d,Dumper=Dumper,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Updated and validated final-angle hypothesis:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
