{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_33", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r9s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r9s2',\n'title':'Predict unsigned narrow load forwarding and validate at MEM/WB',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion scores 203.36 at median Gowin Fmax 85.344 MHz and\n4,196,601 bracketed CoreMark cycles. Its worst 17.775 ns path starts at\ndata-memory bank 3 and ends at OC alu_b_val bit 29, through load formatting\nand forwarding. This points to high-bit/sign-extension propagation on the\naccepted MEM-load bypass. LESSONS.md is absent; predictor history was\nreviewed. Bimodal/JAL and narrow MUL prediction won, while carry/shift\nprediction, smaller MULs and delayed branch recovery failed acceptance.\nThe most direct remaining predictor opportunity is to remove high memory\ndata bits from speculative load forwarding, preserving full exact loads\nbehind the existing registered recovery boundary.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one stateless computational load-value predictor used only by the\nMEM-to-OC forwarding path. For byte loads predict the selected byte\nzero-extended to 32 bits; for halfword loads predict the selected halfword\nzero-extended to 32 bits; for word loads predict {12'b0, dmem_rdata[19:0]}.\nByte/halfword lane selection uses the true registered effective address,\nand access-width selection remains exact. LB/LH deliberately predict a\nnonnegative result; LBU/LHU predictions are exact. LW predicts that bits\n31:20 are zero. Declare and construct these widths explicitly, independently\nof load_data, so synthesis cannot implement the predictor as truncation\nafter the existing sign-extension/result mux. All predicted bits 31:20\nare constant zero. There is no history table, confidence policy, extra\narithmetic, fetch predictor change or speculative effective address.\n\nPreserve EX's unavailable-load interlock and the current single load-use\nbubble. Only after the true MEM load handshake is ready may the nearest\nload producer supply this candidate to OC. Use the existing valid,\npost-alignment-trap, nonzero-destination writer and readiness qualification.\nChange MEM bypass_value for loads to the unsigned/narrow candidate; keep\nordinary ALU and multiply bypasses intact. Neither a predicted load nor a\nconsumer may bypass memory backpressure. Never move memory data into EX\nor add a combinational feedback path through current execution.\n\nKeep the entire exact memory datapath for MEM/WB and architectural\nwriteback: all load widths, signed and unsigned extension, raw RVFI memory\nword, masks, full original source values and full destination value.\nValidate the candidate against the exact load_data for each accepted legal\naligned load that writes a nonzero destination. Register its mismatch into\nthe existing MEM/WB older-repair bit, ORed with multiply mismatch. Use\nseparate qualified load and multiplication comparisons, rather than a\nshared predicted/exact result mux before equality. Preserve the independent\nrepair-target capture from in.pc_next, which is PC+4 for loads. A comparator\nmust have no same-cycle fanout into OC capture, memory outputs or recovery;\nonly the registered older-repair bit controls those effects.\n\nReuse the existing precise registered recovery unchanged. A mismatching\nload retires once and writes its exact value while the next-cycle repair\nredirects to its PC+4. Quarantine every younger MEM request even if its bus\nis unready; squash younger EX/OC/decode work, flush retained OC sources,\nsuppress younger EX redirects/training/divider launch, and cancel a younger\nactive or completed divider. Correct predictions introduce no new bubble.\nStores and addresses remain exact; an incorrect load value cannot become\na memory side effect or retirement. Treat valid/ready/alignment/write\nqualification identically during holds so a waiting load never repairs or\nretires twice. Loads to x0 need no repair. Prediction assumptions never\nbecome operand restrictions, bounds checks, decoder legality or trap rules.\n\nA fresh architectural profile of the unchanged canonical 2K, -O3,\nten-iteration ELF completed 2,937,037 instructions, with all five canonical\nCRCs and the validation literal, and no out-of-bounds access. Between the\nmarkers, 535,154 of 544,852 load candidates match (98.2201%). Misses are\n3,180 of 270,342 LW, 6,438 of 167,580 LH and 80 of 1,830 LB; all 105,100\nunsigned byte/halfword loads match. These are ISS value classifications,\nnot RTL timing or recovery measurements. Three to four added cycles per\n9,698 miss would add about 0.69 to 0.92 percent to the champion's measured\ncycles, before actual stall overlap and replay effects. Removing the\nmemory-to-high-OC-bit path could therefore support a useful Fmax gain\nwithout a large replay cost. Remaining low-bit extraction, EX return\nbypass and exact-load-to-WB paths can become the new timing limits.\n\nKeep nret=1, all top-level ports, pipeline topology, branch prediction,\nfull and ALTOPS arithmetic, decoder defaults and every invariant/check.\nVerify unsigned boundaries around 2\"'^20, arbitrary 32-bit LW values,\nnegative LB/LH, all aligned lanes, x0 and alignment traps. Force mismatches\nwith younger ALU/load/store/branch/JALR/DIV/REM consumers, simultaneous\nunrelated MEM work, retained operands and independent bus stalls. Preserve\nall architectural assertions; adapt only predictor-policy-specific load\nbypass expectations. Run unchanged formal and ready/stalled trace cosim,\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRC/bracket validation and median vendor Gowin\ntiming. Acceptance requires (Fmax_new/85.344)*(4,196,601/cycles_new)>1.046;\nwith one percent more cycles, Fmax must exceed about 90.16 MHz. The stated\neight-percent expected gain is a hypothesis, not an accepted measurement.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Construct a separate unsigned/narrow load candidate directly from the\ntrue selected byte/halfword or low 20 bits of the raw word. Forward it\nonly on the existing qualified accepted-load bypass. Keep exact load_data\nand every architectural memory/RVFI field. Register valid legal aligned\nnonzero-rd load mismatches into the existing older multiply recovery,\nusing independent comparisons and the stored pc_next target. Preserve\nall hold, quarantine, exact multiplication and WB semantics.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_mem_repair.py','description':'''Retain all exact-multiply and recovery checks and add direct load\ncandidate/commit tests for each width and lane, unsigned-20-bit word\nboundaries, negative signed loads, arbitrary full values, x0, invalid and\ntrapping accesses, dmem holds and quarantine. Check exact read_data,\noriginal RVFI payload, candidate readiness and one-shot registered repair.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Retain every architectural/forwarding/order/trap/memory assertion. Adapt\nonly expectations that require exact speculative MEM load forwarding.\nExercise correct candidates without added bubbles and forced failures\nwith dependent ALU, load, store, branch, JALR and divider consumers;\nverify exact original-load retirement and younger replay, canceled divide,\nretained-source clearing, independent bus stalls and older MUL priority.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(d,json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert type(d['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nprint('Replaced hypothesis with schema-valid unsigned/narrow load prediction')\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
