{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml,json,jsonschema\np=Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261005-003-r9s2.yaml')\nd={\n'id':'hyp-20261005-003-r9s2',\n'title':'Predict MEM load values from a tagged word history and wait for WB on misses',\n'category':'predictor',\n'motivation':'''The champion reaches 203.36 at 85.344 MHz with 4,196,601 bracketed\nCoreMark cycles. Its worst 17.775 ns path runs from data-memory bank 3\nthrough MEM formatting and forwarding to OC alu_b_val bit 29. LESSONS.md\nis absent and predictor history was reviewed. Earlier bimodal/JAL and\nnarrow MUL prediction won; delayed branch validation and weaker arithmetic\npredictions failed acceptance. A load-value predictor can replace the slow\nraw-memory bypass with a small local table while retaining every memory\nrequest and exact retirement. A fresh unsigned/narrow-load probe measured\nonly 79.721 MHz, so this proposal removes the entire raw MEM-to-OC bypass,\nincluding the fallback path, rather than just its upper bits.\n''',\n'hypothesis':'''Add one address-tagged load-value predictor at MEM: a 128-entry\ndirect-mapped history of previously observed raw memory words. Index by\nregistered effective_addr[8:2], tag with all effective_addr[31:9], and store\n32 raw data bits plus a valid bit. Reset valid bits only; do not reset tags\nor data, allowing distributed LUT-RAM inference. Mask invalid lookup\nqualification so unknown payloads never become a ready forwarding source.\nLook up from the existing EX/MEM address register, with no current EX\naddress adder or forwarding mux before the lookup. Inspect actual Gowin\ninference; the table must not become a slow block-RAM read or a large\nresettable register mux without measuring that cost.\n\nFor a qualified legal aligned load with a matching valid tag, format the\npredicted word using the true address lane, width and signedness and feed\nthat candidate to the existing MEM-to-OC bypass. Qualify readiness with the\nactual dmemReady handshake and existing final writer eligibility. On a\nmiss, keep the matching MEM producer unavailable: OC waits until the exact\nload value is registered in MEM/WB and forwards from WB on the next cycle.\nNever select live dmemRData as a fallback MEM-to-OC value. Maintain EX's\nunavailable-load interlock and nearest-writer priority. Hits preserve the\ncurrent one load-use bubble; misses can cost one additional bubble for a\nwaiting consumer. No prediction bypasses or shortens a memory transaction,\nchanges an address, skips a request or authorizes a store.\n\nEvery load still reads the original bus and commits its exact extracted\nvalue at MEM/WB. Validate a used prediction by comparing its raw predicted\nword directly with raw dmemRData on an accepted load, independently of\nload formatting. Full-word equality is a sufficient certificate for every\nload width and sign; conservatively replay if only unused bytes differ.\nGate mismatch by hit, valid accepted legal aligned load, reg_write and\nrd\"'!=x0. Register mismatch into the existing MEM/WB older-repair bit,\nORed with the independently qualified multiply mismatch. Do not put a\nshared result-selection mux ahead of equality, or let the comparator\ncontrol same-cycle OC forwarding, frontend recovery or memory outputs.\nCapture the stored pc_next repair target independently, as today.\n\nReuse registered older recovery precisely. A failed prediction retires\nthe original load once with exact data; next-cycle repair redirects to its\nPC+4, quarantines younger MEM requests even when unready, squashes younger\nEX/OC/decode work and retained sources, suppresses younger branch training\nand redirects, and cancels a younger divider or held completion. Correct\nhits add no bubble. x0 needs no replay. All original operand, trap, mask,\nraw-memory RVFI and consecutive retirement-order fields remain exact.\nMiss waiting is an ordinary unavailable-source hold, not a squash or a\nwhole-pipeline memory stall.\n\nLearn only from accepted nonquarantined legal memory operations. A load\nfills/replaces its entry with the actual full raw memory word, including\non a prediction failure. An accepted full-word store allocates/replaces\nwith the exact stored word. An accepted partial store merges enabled bytes\ninto a matching entry; on a tag miss it does not allocate unknown remaining\nbytes. Preserve same-edge pre-write lookup semantics. All updates are\nqualified by valid, alignment, dmemReady, !hold_wb and !older_repair;\nwaiting requests never write repeatedly and wrong-path stores never train.\nDo not add reset to payload arrays. The value history is advisory: external\nmemory changes, stale entries and arbitrary loaded values always remain\nsafe because the real bus word validates every used prediction. This is\none load-value prediction mechanism, with no memory-request hit bypass,\nfetch predictor change, arithmetic prediction change or pipeline split.\n\nAn architectural replay of the unchanged canonical 2K, -O3, ten-iteration\nELF finds 514,383 matching address entries out of 544,852 bracketed loads\nwith this 128-entry update policy, about 94.4 percent coverage. All those\nformatted candidates match; 30,469 accesses miss and only 3,364 misses have\nan immediate raw-register-field consumer. These are sequential reference\nprofiles, not RTL timing, cycle counts or a proof of prediction correctness.\nPipeline timing and independent stall phases can change both waiting and\ncoverage. The full reference run completes 2,937,037 instructions, has no\nout-of-bounds accesses, and emits all five canonical CRCs plus the validation\nliteral. A small extra miss-wait cost could be offset by removing the timed\nBRAM-data-to-OC cone. Table/tag mux routing, predictor-to-OC formatting,\nexact-load-to-WB timing and the EX-result return bypass are the main risks.\n\nPreserve nret=1, every top-level port, all branch and arithmetic policies,\nreal/ALTOPS behavior, divider protocol, decoder defaults and all invariants.\nDo not change benchmark, wrapper, timing, stall-generation or formal files.\nVerify reset/miss masking, full-tag aliases, all load widths and lanes,\npartial-store merges, changed bus values on a valid hit, arbitrary signed\nand unsigned words, x0, misalignment, same-index read/write and dmem holds.\nForce stale prediction recovery with dependent ALU/load/store/branch/JALR/\nDIV/REM work, unrelated younger MEM effects, retained operands and older\nmultiply repair. Preserve every architectural assertion; adapt only checks\nthat assume a ready exact MEM bypass on a history miss. Run unchanged\nformal, ready/stalled trace cosims, canonical stalled CoreMark CRC/bracket\nvalidation and median vendor timing. Acceptance requires\n(Fmax_new/85.344)*(4,196,601/cycles_new)>1.046. The expected eight-percent\nfitness gain remains an estimate pending final implementation and evaluation.\n'\"''',\n'expected_impact':{'fitness_delta_pct':8,'confidence':'low'},\n'changes':[\n {'file':'rtl/load_value_predictor.sv','description':'''Add a 128-entry address-tagged raw-word value history, asynchronous\nregistered-address lookup, valid-only reset and one accepted memory update\nper cycle. Loads and full-word stores replace entries; partial stores\nmerge matching byte lanes. Mask invalid qualification and preserve\npre-write reads. Keep all payload arrays unreset for LUT-RAM inference.\n'''},\n {'file':'rtl/mem_stage.sv','description':'''Instantiate the history locally from registered effective addresses.\nFormat predicted words for MEM-to-OC load forwarding; tag misses make that\nproducer unavailable until exact WB, with no live-memory fallback. Keep\nactual memory requests and exact MEM/WB data. Validate raw predicted word\nagainst the accepted raw bus word and register mismatches through existing\nolder recovery with precise quarantine. Learn only accepted aligned legal\nnonquarantined loads/stores. Preserve multiplier and all held WB semantics.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_load_value_predictor.py','description':'''Add reset and unknown-payload masking, full-address tag aliases,\nreplacement, load filling, full/partial store learning, disabled/held\nupdates and same-index pre-write checks for the local history module.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_mem_repair.py','description':'''Retain existing exact-multiply, hold and quarantine assertions. Add load\nhistory hits/misses, candidate formatting for all widths/signs/lanes,\nx0 and trapping accesses, disabled readiness on misses, exact WB results,\nforced stale-word mismatch and one-shot registered repair during bus holds.\n'''},\n {'file':'test/test_pipeline.py','description':'''Include the added RTL module in explicit runner lists. Preserve all\narchitectural, memory, RVFI-order, forwarding, arithmetic and trap checks.\nAdapt readiness expectations for history misses and exercise WB fallback,\nnearest producer blocking, retained sources, coherent store learning,\nforced stale hits with every dependent consumer class, wrong-path stores,\ncanceled divides, independent bus stalls and older multiplication priority.\n'''}]\n}\np.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,sort_keys=False,width=90))\njsonschema.validate(yaml.safe_load(p.read_text()),json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nprint('Final angle written and schema validated:',p)\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
